  {"a":"olaf","b":"aatrox","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"You can fight at level 1 — Q-slow into autos punishes him before his Q knockups and chain-pull come online, since he is weakest levels 1-2."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R (World Ender) is his real spike — more healing, AD and Move Speed. Ragnarok gives resists and disable-immunity, not sustain, so it loses the long fight."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His drain-tank core (Goredrive/Eclipse) tips extended trades his way; your E true damage helps but his W-pull + sweetspot Q out-sustain you over time."},{"when":"Late","text":"It evens back out — your E true damage still bites his tanky build, but his teamfight knockups outscale your flat dive; trade picks, don't 1v1 a ulted Aatrox."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q on his approach and chain the axe pickup to perma-slow him so his sweetspot Q whiffs","Keep every trade SHORT — burst with E true damage and W-omnivamp, then walk before his passive heal-on-hit and drain stack up","Abuse levels 1-2 and bait his Q knockup, then all-in while it is on cooldown"],"foe":["Drag you into long trades where his passive heal-on-hit and W-pull out-sustain your W-omnivamp","Land sweetspot Q knockups and chain-pull you into his combo while you are slowed","Hit 6 and pop R (World Ender) to win the extended all-in and any tower dive"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours — he is one of the weakest early champs and you are one of the strongest. Open with Q to slow him, walk up for autos as your passive attack speed ramps, and pick the axe back up to keep him slowed so his sweetspot Q (the edge of the swing that knocks up) keeps missing. Dodge the center of his Q and never stand in a minion line where his W chain-pull can drag you into a full combo. If you land E true damage on a short trade here, you win it outright.","mid":"From level 3 the lane tilts to him because his Q rotation and passive heal-on-hit turn every prolonged fight into a drain war that your W-omnivamp loses over time. Keep trades short and explosive — Q-slow, E true-damage nuke, auto, leave — and refuse to stand and brawl. At 6 his R is the bigger spike: World Ender heals him and boosts his combat stats, so your Ragnarok-immunity all-in does NOT out-DPS a fully ulted Aatrox. Only commit if his R is down or you have jungle help.","late":"It levels back out. Your E true damage still cuts his drain-tank build, so you stay relevant in skirmishes, but a fully built Aatrox with R up wins the straight 1v1 — his knockups and self-heal beat your flat dive once you fall off at 2+ items. Don't ego the solo duel into his ult; instead use your Q-slow and Ragnarok to dive HIS backline in teamfights while he is committed to your frontline. Convert your early lead into towers and objectives before this window.","whys":["You both fight at 1, but your Q-slow-into-auto and ramping passive beat his sweetspot Q before his combo exists — it is genuinely even, edge to whoever lands first.","Your level-2 Q+E burst trades evenly with his early kit; he is weak levels 1-2 so neither of you fully owns it.","From 3 his Q rotation and passive heal-on-hit start winning the extended trades your short burst can't out-sustain.","His W-pull plus drain stacking out-heals your W-omnivamp in any prolonged fight through 4-5.","World Ender boosts his healing, AD and speed — Ragnarok gives immunity to disables, not sustain.","His drain-tank core tips long trades his way; your E true damage helps but doesn't reclaim the lane.","Your E true damage still bites his tanky build and your dive stays relevant — it evens back out into a pick-trading skirmish."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"akali","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Olaf","Skill","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into auto plus E true damage chunks her before she has Shroud up to hide in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R two-part dash plus shuriken execute outranges your all-in and she can reset through Shroud — her first real kill threat."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once she finishes Hextech Rocketbelt / Cosmic Drive she dashes in, bursts, and Shrouds before you can land E."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full AP Akali blinks your Q and resets fights with R — convert your early lead before 2 items or she takes over."}],"wants":{"you":["Slow with Q — it passes through Shroud — and land E true damage before her 16s W is back","Force short all-ins at Levels 2-3 where Berserker Rage lifesteal and the W shield out-trade her energy poke","End the lane on your first-item spike before her R and AP items come online"],"foe":["Drop W Twilight Shroud to dodge your targeted E; the Q axe still passes through her","Hit Level 6 R for a two-part dash reset and execute over your all-in","Stack AP items so she can blink your Q and burst you before you commit"]},"early":"Akali has no Shroud charge wasted yet and her energy pool is shallow, so Levels 1-3 are yours. Land Q to slow her, walk up, and weave an auto plus E true damage — that point-blank nuke can't be dodged by her dash the way a skillshot can, and it eats her low early HP. Berserker Rage ramps attack speed and lifesteal as her shurikens chip you, and Tough It Out shields the rest, so every short trade nets out your way. Never dump E into a fresh Shroud — it cannot select her; bait the 16s W first.","mid":"Through Levels 4-5 you still win the short all-in: chain Q axe pickups to perma-slow her so she can't kite, and Shroud only buys seconds — your Q still lands inside it while the W shield and passive lifesteal grind her down. Level 6 flips it: Perfect Execution is a two-part dash that closes or escapes and finishes with an execute, and Ragnarok's disable-immunity answers none of it. Trade only while her 120/90/60s R is down.","late":"Once Akali has a completed AP item plus R she dashes in, bursts, and is untargetable in Shroud before your E lands — your flat true damage and short-fight kit stop being enough. This is a snowball-or-fade lane: your whole game is the early-to-first-item window. Take plates, dives, and grubs/herald with your tempo, because at 2+ items she out-resets and out-bursts you and the duel is no longer yours.","whys":["Q-slow into auto wins first contact and your passive out-DPSes her empty-energy poke before she has anything to hide behind.","With Q plus E you land a guaranteed true-damage chunk she can't dodge with a dash, and her HP pool is too low to answer.","Chained Q axe pickups perma-slow her into your E while Tough It Out shields the shuriken poke — a short all-in here is yours.","Even — you still out-trade with sustain, but her Shroud lets her dodge a committed E and break even on the exchange.","Her R two-part dash plus execute outranges and resets through your all-in, turning your engage into her kill window.","Her first AP item gives her the burst to dash in, blow you up, and Shroud before your E comes back — she edges the lane now.","Full-build Akali blinks your Q and resets fights with R while you fall off, so this window is a coinflip you must avoid by ending early."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"akshan","win":["Akshan","Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Akshan","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Land Q to slow him and walk him down with passive attack-speed autos before he has E to grapple away."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks him hard if you catch him without an E-swing charge off terrain."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Akshan has no CC for Ragnarok to ignore — its value at 6 is resists plus the uninterrupted run-down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His Black Cleaver / lethality spike lets him kite-poke you down between trades — his biggest threat window."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q on him and immediately auto so the slow lets you stick and stack passive attack speed","Bait his 18s E grapple out, then Reckless Swing him and shield the answer with Tough It Out","Save Ragnarok for the run-down and all-in at 6 before his lethality items come online"],"foe":["Keep E-swing charges off terrain to dash out the instant you commit a Q","Poke you with Q+passive procs and disengage so your true damage never lands","Roam with camouflage and scale his lethality build to kite you from range"]},"early":"Akshan can't trade with you levels 1-3 if you land Q — the slow sticks him and your passive ramps attack speed as you take his poke, so short trades go your way and your E true damage cuts a chunk he can't heal back. Don't throw Q at max range where he just walks out of it; throw it as he steps up to last-hit, then auto. Watch his E grapple — if he has a charge off the wall behind him he'll swing out of your all-in, so push him off his terrain first.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a coinflip — his Avengerang rhythm and lethality come online, and if you whiff Q he chunks you for free between your cooldowns. At 6 Ragnarok is the equalizer, but not by breaking CC: Akshan has none. It is the resists and the run-down nothing interrupts, so land Undertow at his feet and pick the axe up for the reset. Use it while he stands with no terrain behind him. Don't ult into nothing — bait the 18s grapple first.","late":"Once his lethality build comes together he'd love to kite-poke you from range and roam with camouflage, but this lane stays even into the late game — Reckless Swing's true damage still ignores his squishy build and Ragnarok still catches him mid-fight. Your job is to convert: take plates and dives while Heroic Swing's 18s is down rather than letting it drag into a poke war where his Q and Dirty Fighting shield whittle you. Don't facecheck his camouflage near objectives.","whys":["Your Q-slow into passive-fueled autos beats his level-1 poke before he has E to grapple away.","He gets Q+W poke rhythm going and chunks you between your cooldowns if you miss a Q.","His lethality starts online and he kite-pokes — without Ragnarok you can't punish his disengage yet.","Pure skill matchup — your Q-catch versus his E-swing dodge decides every trade here.","Even window — Ragnarok's resists let you commit, but Heroic Swing still swings him out of it.","His first lethality item lets him poke you down from range faster than your true damage can close.","You reclaim it — your true damage ignores his squishy build and Ragnarok catches him mid-fight to dive."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"ambessa","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into a Reckless Swing (E) true-damage nuke chunks Ambessa before her W chain combo can punish you back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ambessa's spike: Public Execution suppresses then stuns from 1250 range. Ragnarok answers it — but only if you still have your 100s ult."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / bruiser core with Tough It Out on — your most oppressive all-in window; perma-slow her with axe resets and shield Repudiation's slam."},{"when":"Late","text":"You reclaim 1v1s because your true damage and slows stick on a no-real-escape bruiser, but group up so her chain CC can't isolate you."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick Ambessa with Undertow (Q) slows and pick the axe back up to chain-slow through her dash mobility","Bait Repudiation's braced shield, pop Tough It Out, then Reckless Swing her and take the trade","Save Ragnarok (R) to make her chain CC and ult lock useless when you commit the all-in"],"foe":["Weave around your Undertow (Q) with her dash combo so your slow never sticks and her W lands clean","Hit Level 6 and catch you with her R + chain CC during a trade where your Ragnarok is down","Drag the game even and scale her bruiser build into teamfights where she can isolate you"]},"early":"Ambessa wants to weave her dash combo around your Undertow (Q), so don't waste the axe on a panic throw — lead with it to land the slow, then walk up and pick it back up to keep her stuck. Once she's slowed, your Reckless Swing (E) true damage cuts straight through her bruiser stats and she can't dash out of a slow she's already eating. At Levels 2-3 you out-burst her hard; just respect that her W combo hits back if you flail in without the slow landing first.","mid":"Through 4-5 you stay ahead — short trades with axe-reset slows plus the Tough It Out shield absorb anything Repudiation chips off you, and she has no sustain to match. Level 6 is HER window: Public Execution blinks 1250 units, suppresses, then stuns, so do NOT all-in into it unless your Ragnarok (R) is up. If you have R, you flip it — pop it, the suppress does nothing, and run her down with the slow and E.","late":"You reclaim the straight 1v1 because her Drakehound's Step dashes are short — your slows stick, Reckless Swing's true damage ignores her armour, and Berserker Rage's missing-health lifesteal outlasts her. The danger is being isolated and suppressed by Public Execution before you reach her. Group with your team, force the all-in while Ragnarok is up, and never let her combo onto you slowed and Rless.","whys":["Your Undertow slow into an auto wins first contact — Ambessa's dash combo can't kite a slow she's standing in at Level 1.","Q-slow into Reckless Swing (E) true damage chunks her before her W combo comes back online.","Even window — she can now weave her full dash combo around a single Q, so the trade comes down to whether your slow lands or her W does.","Axe-reset slows plus the Tough It Out shield out-trade her combos and eat Repudiation's chip — she has no sustain.","Ambessa owns 6: Public Execution suppresses you from 1250 range, and with Ragnarok's 100s down there is no answer to it.","Skill window — your bruiser first item trades even with her scaling combo; it comes down to who lands their engage cleanly.","You reclaim the 1v1 — her stats can't outrun your slows and E true damage, and Berserker Rage wins the extended fight."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"aurora","win":["Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Aurora","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Lead with a max-range Undertow (Q) so the slow sticks before she can angle her E blink away, then walk on for a free auto."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok gives resists and disable-immunity, but Aurora's crowd control is slows — it frees nothing. Its value is surviving her burst."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Bramble/Cleaver and Tough It Out's shield you absorb her Q poke in a sustained trade, but only if you caught The Weirding's 15s down."},{"when":"Lvl 2-5","text":"Her threat window: she Q-pokes you to half then E-blinks the instant you throw an axe, refusing the melee all-in your passive needs."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Undertow (Q) on her before she E-blinks so the slow lets you stick and stack autos with your low-HP attack-speed passive","Hold Ragnarok for after she commits The Weirding's hop, then dive while she has no second escape ready","Force the melee all-in at 1st item where Vicious Strikes (W) omnivamp out-heals her poke"],"foe":["Poke you with Twofold Hex's out-and-back curse and never let you close the gap","Save E to blink away the moment you commit Q or walk in, then re-poke from safety","Bait your Ragnarok early, then Across the Veil out of range and burst you once it drops"]},"early":"Level 1 is close if I lead with a tip-range Undertow — the axe slow can stick her before she reads it and hops with The Weirding, and I walk up for a free auto with my passive already ticking. But the second she hits 2 and 3 it flips: Twofold Hex curses on the way out and is recast to drag back through me, and the instant I throw a Q she hops the gap and I've spent the slow on air. Don't chase into her minions for a refunded axe — that is where the recast lands and the poke adds up. Farm, hold Q for when she commits forward.","mid":"Levels 4-6 she edges me because my whole kit wants a melee all-in and The Weirding's slow-and-hop keeps refusing it. The mistake is expecting Ragnarok to fix that — her crowd control is slows, not disables, so the immunity frees nothing; what it buys is armour, MR and an uninterrupted run-down. Bait the hop first: walk in like I'm committing, make her burn the 15s E, THEN Q-slow and R-dive while she has no second escape. Tough It Out only matters if I land hits, so the lane is one clean stick.","late":"This is the one window that's mine. Aurora is a squishy skirmish-mage, and once I have a couple of bruiser items Reckless Swing's true damage cuts her whatever she builds and Ragnarok's armour and MR carry me through the burst — she can't kite me the way a real ranged hypercarry can. I have to convert here, though: I'm not a true scaler, so I want to be ending the game on her, not waiting. Catch her sided and let Tough It Out's shield cover the poke as I close.","whys":["My level-1 Undertow slow can land before she hops with The Weirding, but she can also just step back — first contact is a coinflip here.","She hits 2 first in lane tempo here and Q-pokes from blink range — every time I throw an axe to engage she just E-blinks the gap.","Twofold Hex's recast and The Weirding's slow chip me faster than I can close, and my W shield does nothing at range.","Through 4-5 she keeps E-blinking my engage and re-poking, so I bleed health without ever landing the stick my all-in needs.","Her 6 arrives too: Between Worlds slows and repositions her, and Across the Veil takes her invisible out of my reach.","At her first item the poke-and-blink pattern is at its strongest — she pressures my health bar while staying outside my Q range.","Now my bruiser items plus E true damage and Ragnarok let me dive through her root and delete a squishy mage who can't kite me unstoppable."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"camille","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Land Q-slow into an auto at first contact — Camille has no Hookshot yet to escape the slow, so first blood pressure is yours."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once Camille has E she wall-dashes out of your Q-slow and knocks you up on landing — the 16s Hookshot is the early danger."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's disable-immunity beats Hookshot's knockup while you keep attacking — pop it and swing through her reset."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Camille's true-damage Q proc and W heal scale past your flat E; convert before her item spikes or she duels you out."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick a Camille with chained Q-slows so her E hookshot and W dash can't reset the trade","All-in under Ragnarok so Hookshot's knockup can't stop you, with Tough It Out covering her burst","Snowball levels 1 and 6 into a lead before her two-item Q/W true-damage scaling arrives"],"foe":["Use Hookshot's wall-dash knockup to dodge your Q axe and reset every trade on her terms","Land Tactical Sweep's outer half for the heal and Q's true-damage reset to win long duels","Stall to two items so her Adaptive Defenses shield and true damage out-scale your flat E"]},"early":"Camille has no Hookshot at level 1, so first contact is yours — sling Undertow to slow her, walk up for the auto, and let Berserker Rage attack speed punish her. The moment she hits 2 and has E, the lane shifts: she can wall-dash straight out of your Q-slow and knock you up on the landing, so don't blow your axe when she's hugging a wall. Pick the axe up to refund Q and keep her slowed, but respect that the 16s Hookshot is now what turns a trade against you.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are hers to bully if you misstep — Hookshot's knockup plus Tactical Sweep's outer-half heal let her win short trades and reset on the wall before your slow sticks. Hold your tempo for 6: Ragnarok makes that knockup useless while you keep attacking, so Reckless Swing's true damage and the Tough It Out shield carry the all-in. That ult-up moment is your cleanest kill all lane — bait her E, then commit when Ragnarok is live.","late":"This is Camille's game, not yours. Her Q true-damage proc and W heal scale past your flat E true-damage chunk, and her Adaptive Defenses shield blunts your all-in once she's two items deep. Don't try to outduel a fed Camille in a sidelane — your kit loses value as her items come online. Convert the early-and-six leads into towers, dives and objectives before then, and let your team handle her R-isolation pick threat in the mid game.","whys":["Camille has no E hookshot stun at level 1 — your Q-slow into auto and Berserker Rage win first contact before she can dodge or reset.","Once she has E she can wall-dash out of your Q and stun you, but your Q-reset slow and W trade keep it genuinely even.","With E up Camille hookshot-stuns and wall-dashes to dodge your axe and reset trades on her terms — her window edges yours.","Hookshot's knockup plus Tactical Sweep's outer-half heal out-trade your short combo through 4-5, before your ult.","Ragnarok makes Hookshot's knockup and her slows useless while you keep swinging — with the Tough It Out shield, 6 is a coinflip.","Even with your bruiser first item, her true-damage Q proc and Adaptive Defenses shield let her reset and out-duel you.","She hard-outscales: her two-item Q/W true damage and heal kite and burst you, so close it before her items if you can — but the early lead is yours to bank."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia","Skill","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Land Undertow on the wave and walk her down — your passive attack speed plus a Q-slow auto wins first contact before she has poison stacks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok is immune to her R stun but not her slows — Miasma still kites you, though its grounding does nothing to you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Black Cleaver / Bramble core you sit on her with perma-Q slows while Tough It Out shields the poison ticks — your most oppressive all-in window."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Cassiopeia hits Liandry's / Rylai's she kites you with grounding and Twin Fang DPS faster than your flat true damage can answer — her takeover."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Undertow to stick the slow, pick the axe back up, and chain throws so she can never kite to poison range","Bait her R stun — Miasma's grounding can't touch a dashless Olaf — then Ragnarok in and Reckless Swing","Snowball levels 1-5 and dive behind the Tough It Out shield before her 2-item poison DPS lands"],"foe":["Keep max range, stack Q/W poison and chunk you before you commit a trade","Land W (Miasma) to slow you out of range and kite the whole all-in","Hit her R face-stun while you are not in Ragnarok, then scale to Liandry's/Rylai's and out-DPS you"]},"early":"Cassiopeia is one of the worst level-1 champions in the game and you are one of the best, so step up immediately — throw Undertow on the wave to land a slow, then walk in for a Q-slowed auto while your passive attack speed climbs. She has no poke that out-damages a committed melee trade this early, and no escape: her W grounding and R stun don't exist yet. Don't over-extend past river on her poison stacks alone, but every time she steps to last-hit, axe-slow her and punish.","mid":"Levels 3-5 Miasma comes online — but grounding only shuts off movement abilities and Olaf has none, so what actually hurts you is its slow. Chain Undertow slows to close on foot and bait the 24s W before you all-in. At 6 Ragnarok answers half her kit: it is immune to Petrifying Gaze's stun, though not to her slows, so R-walk her down and Reckless Swing for the guaranteed true-damage chunk while Tough It Out shields the poison ticks.","late":"This is where she takes the lane back, so don't let it get here even. Once Cassiopeia finishes Liandry's and Rylai's her Twin Fang DPS and perma-slow out-trade you — your flat E true damage stops scaling while her poison percent-HP burn rips through your bruiser HP. If you're behind, your Ragnarok cooldown can't cover every engage and she'll just R-stun you the moment it's down. Convert your early-to-mid lead into towers and dives before two items, or hand her the game.","whys":["She is a bottom-tier level-1 and you are top-tier — Undertow slow into a passive-fueled auto wins first contact before she has a single poison stack.","Her Q poke starts to sting once she has stacks, but a committed Q-slow trade still out-damages it — genuinely even as she finds range.","With W grounding online she cancels your gap-close and kites your axe to poison range — she edges this window before your 6 spike.","You out-trade a pre-item Cassiopeia in short bursts, but her grounding plus your dependence on Ragnarok being up keeps it skill-tested.","Ragnarok ignores her R stun but not her W slow, so you can dive — a clean flash-R or a well-placed Miasma still denies it. Read-dependent.","Your Black Cleaver / Bramble all-in is oppressive with perma-slows, yet her first poison item lets her trade poke for your true damage — a coin-flip on positioning.","Liandry's and Rylai's let her perma-slow and out-DPS your flat true damage — but if you snowballed she can still be too far behind to kite you, so it stays skill."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"chogath","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Cho'Gath","Skill","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q to perma-slow and E's guaranteed true damage online, you can land a full burst combo before Cho'Gath has the bulk to absorb it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Cho'Gath's R is percent-HP true damage — Ragnarok's bonus armour and MR are worth nothing against it, which is exactly why level 6 is his real kill window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble online: your axe-reset slows stick him and E shreds his stacking HP — your most oppressive lane-pressure point."},{"when":"Late","text":"Feast-stacked Cho'Gath plus R execute out-tanks your flat true damage; group and let your E pick early picks before 2 items."}],"wants":{"you":["Chain Q axe-pickups to perma-slow Cho before he can land his Q knockup","Trade short with Reckless Swing and the W shield so his 11s Feral Scream is wasted","Snowball levels 1-6 and force dives before his Feast stacks and R execute scale"],"foe":["Land Q knockup into W silence to stop your E burst and lock you for jungler","Stack Feast HP and farm safely until his percent-HP R execute beats your kit","Drag the lane to 2+ items where his tankiness outlasts your short all-ins"]},"early":"Cho'Gath is a slow, immobile melee with no escape, which is exactly your prey early. Hit Q on him and pick the axe back up to refund the cooldown so the slow never drops, then walk him down with autos as your passive ramps. His only answers are the Q knockup and W silence, so step in AFTER you bait those, then E him for guaranteed true damage he cannot itemize against this early. Don't facecheck his Q in the minion wave or you'll eat the knockup-into-silence and lose the trade.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay close to even because Cho farms Feast stacks and your short trades chip a growing HP pool, but Berserker Rage's missing-health lifesteal holds you level if you trade on his 6s Q. Level 6 flips to him: Ragnarok stops the knockup, but Feast is percent-HP TRUE damage, so the armour and MR it grants are worth nothing — the lower you are, the more surely it finishes you. Don't all-in below half HP at 6; bait the 11s silence and the ult, then commit. After first item Cleaver and Reckless Swing shred his stacks again.","late":"This is Cho'Gath's game, not yours. Feast stacks plus his percent-HP R execute mean your flat true damage and short-fight kit lose value the longer it goes, and he simply out-tanks the all-in. Your job is to have already converted the early-to-mid lead into towers, dives and objectives. In fights, ult onto his carries rather than dueling Cho directly, and never let him get a free R reset on you when you're chunked.","whys":["Cho is one of the slowest, escape-less melees at level 1 — Q-slow into autos wins first contact while your passive ramps attack speed.","At level 2 your Q-reset slow perma-sticks him and he has no dash to peel, so you free-trade before his Feast HP exists.","Level 3 your E true damage lands clean through his bulk and the Tough It Out shield eats the answer back.","Levels 4-5 are even — his Feast stacks absorb your short trades, but Berserker Rage's lifesteal keeps it from tipping.","Cho owns level 6: Feast is percent-HP true damage, so Ragnarok's armour and MR count for nothing — it finishes you when you're chunked.","First item your Black Cleaver and E shred his stacking HP and axe-slows stick him — it edges back even-to-favoured for your all-in.","From 2+ items his Feast bulk and R execute reclaim it, but level-6 dive value plus your kit's early-game ownership keeps the lane even overall."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"darius","win":["Darius","Darius","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Darius"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Darius owns the first all-in: his E pull yanks you in and his bleed-stacked empowered Q outdamages your single Q-slow before you have E."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes you immune to Apprehend while you keep swinging — press it BEFORE the pull, and 6 is your cleanest all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Bramble Vest / Black Cleaver online: Bramble's Grievous Wounds caps his Noxian Might healing and you trade your axe-reset slows into his bleed."},{"when":"Lvl 1-9","text":"Any greedy melee all-in before 6 is his biggest threat — his bleed plus R-execute true damage beats a committed Olaf at low HP."}],"wants":{"you":["Reach 6 and press Ragnarok before his pull lands, then all-in disable-free","Use Q to land axe and pick it up for the cooldown refund, kiting his Q outer-ring sweetspot","Buy Bramble Vest first to cut his Noxian Might healing and out-sustain his bleed"],"foe":["Land his E pull to drag you onto an empowered, bleed-stacked Q before you have R","Stack five Hemorrhage bleeds to trigger Noxian Might and heal through your W","Drop you below the R-execute threshold during any pre-6 melee all-in"]},"early":"Respect Darius levels 1-3 — his E pull plus a bleed-stacked empowered Q outdamages your single Q-slow, and you don't have your Ragnarok escape yet. Don't walk up to throw Q in his E range or he pulls you onto the bleed and wins the trade outright. Last-hit at max Q distance, pick the axe up to refund its cooldown, and chip his health without committing your E true damage while you're full HP and he's stacking Hemorrhage.","mid":"Levels 4-5 tilt your way — short axe-reset trades behind the Tough It Out shield are fine, but never sit in five bleed stacks. Six is your moment: press Ragnarok BEFORE his 26s Apprehend, not after, and the pull cannot land while you keep swinging. Then slow with Q and burn Reckless Swing for the true damage as Berserker Rage ramps. That is the cleanest kill window you get.","late":"This tips his way at items — Bramble Vest is mandatory: its Grievous Wounds caps the Noxian Might healing so Berserker Rage's missing-health lifesteal can out-sustain him in the extended fight. Past two items Noxian Guillotine's true damage keeps scaling off his bleed while your flat true damage does not, so never let it drag to a low-HP melee scrum where his execute beats you. Convert any 6-or-item lead into towers and dives first.","whys":["Darius's E pull drags you onto a bleed-stacked empowered Q and you have no Ragnarok to escape it yet.","His Hemorrhage bleed plus empowered Q still outdamages your lone Q-slow before you've got E for the true-damage burst.","With Q-slow and E true damage online you can match his bleed trade — pick your axe up for the reset and it's a coinflip on positioning.","Short axe-reset trades behind the Tough It Out shield edge it your way — provided you never sit still in five Hemorrhage stacks.","Ragnarok's 100s beats his 120s: press it first and the pull cannot land, so you all-in through his setup and Reckless Swing him.","Bramble's Grievous Wounds caps his Noxian Might healing, so Berserker Rage out-sustains the extended fight and you edge it.","Noxian Guillotine's true damage keeps scaling with his bleed while your flat true damage falls off — the late melee scrum is his."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"drmundo","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Dr. Mundo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once you have Q-slow plus E's true-damage nuke, you out-chunk an early Mundo before his passive heals stack — your peak punish window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's armour and MR let you sit on him through the Heart Zapper burst for a Reckless Swing his resistances cannot reduce."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Bramble Vest plus Black Cleaver is your most oppressive point: grievous wounds cuts his passive/W heal while Cleaver shreds his stacked armor."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His R Maximum Dosage heal and percent-HP Q outscale your flat true damage — this is the window he reclaims and you must already be ahead."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow into auto then E his health bar before his passive regen ticks back up","Buy Bramble/grievous early so antiheal blanks his passive and R heal in every trade","Snowball Levels 1-6 and convert into towers and grubs before he hits 2+ items"],"foe":["Soak your early all-ins and let passive plus Q percent-HP poke heal him back to full","Avoid your E range and Ragnarok all-in, farming until R Maximum Dosage comes online","Drag the game past 2 items where his infinite drain-tank scaling buries your flat damage"]},"early":"Mundo is one of the weakest level-1s and you are the opposite — your Q-slow into auto wins first contact and your passive ramps your attack speed as you take his cleaver poke. Land Q to stick him, walk up, and once you hit 2-3 you E him for guaranteed true damage that his armor and passive regen can't soften. Dodge his Q cleaver throws (they're his only real poke and they cost him health) and punish every miss — he has no escape and no way to answer a committed melee all-in this early.","mid":"This is your strongest stretch — force short trades where the Tough It Out shield eats his Heart Zapper tick and Q-reset slows perma-stick him. The key is anti-heal: rush Bramble Vest so Grievous Wounds cuts his passive regen, and remember the W only heals if its burst catches you — leave the 325 range and he gets nothing. At 6 Ragnarok's armour and MR let you run him down for a Reckless Swing nuke. Force kills now; every plate you take is value he cannot heal away.","late":"Be honest: this flips hard once Mundo finishes 2+ items. His R Maximum Dosage is a massive heal, his Q chunks you for percent-HP, and his bulk means your flat E true damage stops mattering — you can't kill him in a straight fight anymore. Your only path is the lead you built early: take his tower, snowball side lanes, and end the game on objectives before his drain-tank scaling makes him unkillable. If it goes to five items, let your team kite him and you look for the backline with Ragnarok instead of dueling the Mundo.","whys":["Mundo is a famously weak level-1 while your Q-slow-into-auto and passive win first contact outright.","With Q plus E online you land guaranteed true damage his armor and passive regen can't match this early.","He stabilizes slightly as his passive heal and Q percent-HP poke start trading back — close trades go to skill and antiheal timing.","Through 4-5 it is close — his sustain tightens the lane, and whoever respects E range and the Grievous Wounds windows wins the exchange.","Mundo has no disables to ignore — at 6 Ragnarok's armour and MR plus Reckless Swing's true damage carry the dive.","First item is yours — the Bramble/Cleaver spike cuts his heal and shreds armour before his health pool can absorb your damage.","From 2+ items his R Maximum Dosage heal, percent-HP Q, and infinite bulk outscale your true damage — the drain-tank reclaims the lane."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"fiora","win":["Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Skill","Fiora","Fiora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your Q-slow into E true damage is your only real burst window, but Riposte parries the E and slows you mid-combo."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's armour and MR let you eat her Bladework crit and stick a Q-slow, forcing the all-in she normally kites."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver/Bramble is your most oppressive lane point — chain Q resets to perma-slow her before her vitals out-heal you."},{"when":"Late","text":"At 2+ items her passive vitals shred your HP as percent-true while she parries your E — she reclaims the duel hard."}],"wants":{"you":["Force the melee all-in at 6 where Ragnarok's resists hold and her Q dash can't space you out","Bait her W-parry onto a Q or auto, then land E true damage when it is on cooldown","Chain Q axe pickups to perma-slow her so she can't Q-dash to vitals or disengage"],"foe":["Parry your E true damage with W, slow you off it, and flip the trade","Q-dash to your sides to proc passive vitals and dodge your axe","Scale to 2+ items where her Vitals shred percent-HP faster than Berserker Rage heals"]},"early":"This lane starts rough and you have to respect it: from level 1 Riposte flips any trade you lead with — it parries the whole thing, eats your Reckless Swing and slows you off it. Don't lead with the true damage. Farm with Undertow from range and take short trades only when you can track her 24s parry; if she is holding W, your Q+E burst is blanked and she Q-dashes your flank for a free Vital. Through 4-5 her parry timing and Vital healing beat the Tough It Out shield in extended trades, so treat 1-5 as damage control, not a lane to win.","mid":"Level 6 is your one genuinely even window — Ragnarok's armour and MR turn her burst into a brawl, so a stuck Undertow slow into Reckless Swing finally forces the melee all-in she normally kites. That's the play: bait the parry onto a Q or an auto first, then commit R while her 24s W is down. Black Cleaver is your most oppressive point of the game — chain axe pickups to perma-slow her — but it's a snowball check, not a free win: without a lead already banked, her first-item parry plus Vitals still out-trade your spike.","late":"At 2+ items she owns the duel outright — her vitals shred your HP as percent true damage while your flat E true damage falls off, and one parried E flips any fight on the spot. Stop side-laning into her expecting to win the 1v1. Your late value is Ragnarok front-lining: run down her carries in teamfights where the parry can only answer one threat, and only touch Fiora after she's burned W and your team can pile on. If she splits, clear the wave and back off rather than feeding the extended duel she's built to win.","whys":["She W-parries your E true damage outright and slows you off it, so first contact flips if you lead with the nuke.","Your Q+E burst comes online, but a held Riposte blanks the E entirely and slows you — she edges level 2.","She Q-dashes to your flank for a vital proc and resets the short trade faster than your axe can punish at 3.","Through 4-5 her parry timing and Vital healing stay ahead of your Tough It Out shield in long trades.","Ragnarok's resists plus a stuck Undertow slow force the melee all-in she kites — level 6 is genuinely even.","Her first-item parry plus vitals out-trade your Cleaver spike unless you've already snowballed the lane.","At 2+ items her percent-HP true-damage vitals shred you while your flat E true damage falls off — she owns the duel."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"galio","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow into E's true damage you land a guaranteed burst Galio's W shield and base armor can't soak — your first real chunk window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok at 6 shrugs off Shield of Durand's taunt while you keep swinging, but it is a 100s cooldown — spend it on a kill, not on poke."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble online is your peak: perma-slow him with axe resets and E's true damage ignores every point of MR he stacks."},{"when":"Late","text":"Galio scales into a teamfight MR-wall tank — close the lane and convert your lead to towers before his global R makes him a map piece."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow then walk in for E true damage before his W taunt is up","Reset the axe on pickup and shield Winds of War with Tough It Out","Snowball levels 2-6 and dive with R before Galio's MR-stacking makes you tickle him"],"foe":["Land Shield of Durand's taunt and damage reduction to flip your all-in","Poke with Q's wind-blast and passive magic auto when you whiff your axe","Survive lane and use global R to roam, scaling into an MR teamfight wall"]},"early":"Galio's only exit is Justice Punch, an 11-second dash — Undertow grounds it, so drop the axe under him and he cannot step back. Lead with the slow, walk the pickup for the free reset, then weave Reckless Swing in: it is true damage, so his base armor and Shield of Durand's damage reduction do nothing to it. Watch that same W though — the taunt walks you the wrong way, so bait it or trade on its 18s cooldown. His Winds of War poke is real, and your lifesteal grows as your health drops, not from W.","mid":"This is your takeover. Pick up the axe to refund Undertow and keep him permanently slowed, press Tough It Out for attack speed and its shield, and let Reckless Swing's true damage cut whatever MR he builds — your lifesteal climbs the lower you get. At 6 his R is a global engage, not a 1v1 button, and Shield of Durand is his only flip, so bait the taunt on its 14s cooldown and run him down. First item is your hardest oppression window.","late":"Galio's whole identity is scaling into a magic-resist teamfight tank with a game-swinging global R, so the longer this goes the less your flat true damage and short-fight kit matter. You still beat him in the straight 1v1 because E ignores his MR stacking, but he stops dying and starts being a map piece. Win the lane hard levels 2 through first item, take his tower and use your tempo to snowball the map before his R and tankiness turn the game into a 5v5 he's built for.","whys":["Galio is a slow immobile melee with no level-1 escape — your Q-slow into an auto wins first contact outright.","Once you have Q plus E you land a guaranteed true-damage burst his W shield and base armor cannot reduce.","It's a coin-flip on his W taunt: bait it and you stomp the trade, eat it and you walk into his Q poke — play around the taunt timer.","Undertow resets on pickup for perma-slow, and its grounding denies Justice Punch — his only escape.","Galio's R is a global engage; Shield of Durand taunts, but Ragnarok's disable immunity holds while you keep attacking.","Black Cleaver / Bramble is your power peak — E's true damage cuts through every point of MR he stacks and the slow locks him in.","You still win the 1v1 since E ignores his MR, but he scales into a teamfight wall — close the lane before his global R matters."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"gangplank","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Gangplank","Gangplank","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Walk him down with Q-slow into autos before his barrels are online — your passive attack speed ramps as you trade and he has nothing to peel."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep swinging, and no citrus undoes Reckless Swing's true damage — press R for the kill."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once GP gets Sheen/Trinity + barrel chains stacked he out-DPSes your all-in if he hits the full chain — bait the chain, then dash on a fresh stack."},{"when":"Late","text":"His global R and barrel detonations scale past your flat true damage — close the lane before he funds Trinity into Shojin."}],"wants":{"you":["Force melee all-ins early with Q-slow sticking him so he can't reposition to land a barrel chain","Use Tough It Out's shield and your missing-health attack speed to win the extended trade","Snowball levels 1-5 and dive with Ragnarok at 6 before his Trinity/barrel scaling arrives"],"foe":["Stack a 3-barrel chain and detonate it as you commit to E so your trade is net-negative","Use W (Remove Scurvy) to cleanse your Q-slow and walk out of your auto range","Survive to 2+ items and use barrel poke plus global R to scale past your flat true damage"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are yours. His barrels take time to arm and chain, so step on him before he can place a second one — throw Q to slow, walk in, and let your passive attack speed ramp as you trade. He has no dash and no hard CC, so once your axe-slow sticks he physically cannot kite out. Don't stand on a parry-armed barrel; bait it with a feint, then commit. His W (Remove Scurvy) cleanses your Q-slow, so save the big all-in for when it's down.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay close as his barrel chains start hurting if you let him stack three and detonate on your commit — so don't all-in into a primed chain, pick him on a single fresh barrel. At 6 he flips ahead: his W cleanse plus barrel knock-up and citrus heal let him reset a fight you thought you won, and his poke chips your low-econ build between trades. Use your E true damage on cooldown to deny his passive crit autos from winning extended exchanges, but respect that this is where his kit starts answering yours.","late":"Late, Gangplank is the scaler and you are not. Once he funds Trinity Force into Spear of Shojin his barrel detonations crit through your build, his global R impacts other lanes, and your flat E true damage stops mattering as he kites with movement speed and self-peels with W. You have to have already won — convert your level 1-6 lead into towers and dives before ~20 minutes, because past two items he out-ranges, out-poke, and out-scales every all-in you can throw.","whys":["Before his barrels chain you walk him down — Q-slow sticks, autos land, and your passive attack speed ramps with no dash for him to escape.","Your Q-plus-auto into E true-damage burst beats a Gangplank who still only has one barrel and no way to peel.","It's a coinflip once he can place a second barrel — land your axe-slow and you win, eat a fresh chain detonation and you don't.","His three-barrel chain detonation can flip a trade you committed E into, so the lane evens out on whoever respects the other's window.","Level 6 is his — Remove Scurvy cures your Undertow slow and heals the trade on a 22s cooldown, resetting a fight you had won.","His Sheen/Trinity plus stacked barrel chains out-DPS your all-in, and his W self-peel walks him out of your axe range.","His global R, scaling barrel crits and movement-speed kiting overtake your flat true damage — even at best you trade, you no longer dominate."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"gnar","win":["Skill","Gnar","Olaf","Olaf","Gnar","Skill","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E's true-damage nuke online you can stick mini-Gnar and chunk him for a flat burst his boomerang poke can't trade back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep attacking, so Wallop's stun cannot peel you off the all-in — but it costs 100s."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble core makes your axe-reset slows and shielded all-ins oppressive while he is still squishy mini form."},{"when":"Mega bar","text":"His biggest threat: a full Rage bar turning mini into mega for a point-blank AOE stun chains his boomerang and hop to kill you if Ragnarok is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick mini-Gnar with Q-slow and walk him down before he hops away with E","Save Ragnarok for his mega transform so the AOE stun can't lock your all-in","Land Reckless Swing every 11s and let the missing-health passive heal it"],"foe":["Stay mini and kite with boomerang and hops, never giving you a clean Q-stick","Build Rage and time mega's AOE stun for the moment you commit your all-in","Poke you down with boomerang return so you ult into a losing trade"]},"early":"Gnar in mini form is the early annoyance — Boomerang Throw pokes and the return catch chips you, and his Hop means an axe thrown at his feet whiffs if he is already moving. Don't throw Undertow at max range hoping; walk him into a wall or a minion clump, then slow him and close so it sticks. Once you hit 2-3 with Undertow plus Reckless Swing you land a true-damage chunk his poke can't sustain back, and your attack speed ramps as your health drops.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay yours — the axe reset re-throws Undertow off every pickup and perma-sticks him, and your missing-health lifesteal heals through the boomerang chip. The danger is his Rage bar: Wallop's stun locks your all-in and Crunch chains the kill if Ragnarok is down. So read the bar — when he is about to transform, hold R and commit only once you can swing through the stun. With Ragnarok up, Mega is a bigger target you run down.","late":"Your flat true damage and short-fight kit fade as the game goes long, and Gnar scales into a teamfight monster — one Wallop stun on your dive flips a fight. But the 1v1 still favours you if you catch him in mini form on a side lane: Undertow, Reckless Swing, Tough It Out for the shield, Ragnarok so the stun can't hold you. Convert the early-to-mid lead into towers before his frontline value outweighs your picks.","whys":["Mini-Gnar's boomerang pokes but your Q-slow-into-auto and passive answer his first contact — it's a genuine coin-flip skirmish at level 1.","His boomerang return and hops let him kite your single Q before you have E, so he pokes you down and edges the level-2 window.","With Q plus E you stick the slow and land a guaranteed true-damage burst mini-Gnar's poke can't trade against.","The axe reset perma-slows him while your missing-health lifesteal out-heals his boomerang chip.","Mega-Gnar's AOE stun can lock your commit and his hop chains the kill, so the transform window is his to take.","Black Cleaver plus axe-reset slows and W make your all-in oppressive while he's still a squishy mini-form laner.","Your early lead converts here — catch him in mini, Q-slow and E him down while Ragnarok ignores his one peel tool before his mega scaling takes over."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"gragas","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Olaf","Gragas","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Undertow into a Reckless Swing tap out-trades Happy Hour's per-cast healing before he can stack it — your peak window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Explosive Cask is his one out: a 100s knockback that boops you off him or into his jungler, so bait it before you spend Ragnarok on a dive."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver/Bramble online with your axe-reset perma-slow makes you his most oppressive lane bully — force every all-in here."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past 2 items his AP scaling and body-slam disengage matter more, so cash your lead into towers and dives before then."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow then chase the axe pickup to refund cooldown and perma-slow him out of body-slam range","Force short trades where missing-health lifesteal out-paces Happy Hour and Reckless Swing ignores his armour","All-in at 6 with Ragnarok up so his W and slow can't peel you off the kill"],"foe":["Body-slam E away after he chips you, kiting on the slow you can't catch","Spam Q-pool to heal trades and farm at range until his AP items come online","Save R to knock you off him or boop you into his jungler mid-dive"]},"early":"Gragas wants to chip you with Barrel Roll and heal it back with Happy Hour, which only fires when he casts — so his sustain is paced by his mana, not by your damage. Land the axe through him for the slow, then walk in for an auto and Reckless Swing: the true damage ignores his armour, but Drunken Rage still cuts what lands, so swing when that is off. Chase the pickup so Undertow refunds and the slow never drops — that is what stops him Body Slamming away clean. Don't whiff the axe into the minions.","mid":"Through 4-5 you out-trade him on axe-reset slows and missing-health lifesteal — every time he steps up to Barrel Roll, run him down on the slow before Body Slam's 14s is back. Level 6 is the one window where he gets a real answer: Explosive Cask boops you off him or straight into his jungler, so bait it or wait it out before you commit a dive. Then ult, Reckless Swing him out, and Happy Hour will not save the trade.","late":"Once you hit Black Cleaver and a bruiser item with your perma-slow online you're his worst nightmare in lane — this is when you turn every all-in into a kill and crash for plates and dives. But Gragas scales: past 2 items his AP burst and body-slam disengage start to outvalue your flat true damage and short-fight kit. So spend your mid-game lead now — take his tower, dive him with your jungler, and force objectives before his items come online and he can just E away from every fight.","whys":["Your Q-slow-into-auto wins first contact and your passive ramps attack speed as you trade — Gragas has no level-1 burst to match it.","At 2 you add E true damage to the Q-slow, a guaranteed chunk his Q-pool can't out-heal.","Level 3 is genuinely even — he has Q-pool plus body-slam E to disengage and reset, so a missed axe lets him kite the trade out.","Your axe-reset perma-slow and missing-health lifesteal out-grind Happy Hour's per-cast healing in short trades.","Explosive Cask is his one out — a 100s knockback that boops you off him or into his jungler, so he owns the level-6 all-in if you dive it blind.","Black Cleaver plus your perma-slow is your most oppressive point — he can't body-slam away from a target he can never un-slow.","You still beat his bruiser build 1v1, so close it now and dive before his AP scaling and E disengage reclaim the game past two items."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"garen","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Garen","Garen","Olaf","Garen","Garen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Garen edges early contact: his Q silence cancels your axe throw and his W tenacity shrugs the slow, so his empowered strike out-trades your short Q-auto pokes."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok is your one clean window: disable-immune while you keep attacking, so his silence does nothing — ult, Reckless Swing, run him down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His Stridebreaker/bruiser core plus W tenacity lets him disengage your perma-slow again; this is his reclaim point right after your Level 6 spike."},{"when":"Late","text":"Genuinely even — both fall off into team utility; his R missing-HP execute and your dive immunity cancel out in the 1v1."}],"wants":{"you":["Save Ragnarok to strip his Q silence and peel, then E true damage him down at 6","Stick a Q-slow into auto and bait his W tenacity window before committing","Convert your one Level 6 dive into a kill or plate before his item disengage returns"],"foe":["Land Q silence the instant you start your axe throw or E to cancel the cast","Pop W to cut your all-in burst and tenacity through your Q-slow, then disengage","Walk you down with passive regen and finish low trades with R missing-HP execute"]},"early":"Garen owns first contact here in a way most bruisers don't. His Q silences you the moment you wind up an axe throw or E, shutting off your guaranteed true-damage burst, and his W gives tenacity that eats your Undertow slow so you can't perma-stick him. Don't throw Q into auto range expecting him to sit in it — he'll Q-silence-strike and walk off with passive regen healing the trade back. Last-hit, hold your E, and wait for your real window.","mid":"Levels 4-5 still favour him short — Courage's tenacity and the silence beat your axe-reset pattern. But Level 6 is yours: Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune as long as you keep swinging, so ult in, Tough It Out for the shield and attack speed, Reckless Swing for the true-damage chunk, and Undertow to chase. That window is your best chance at a kill or a plate before he reclaims at first item — Stridebreaker and Courage let him disengage your slow again right after.","late":"It evens out completely late — this is a true 50/50. You both fall off into team-utility roles: his R becomes a missing-HP execute pick and your Ragnarok becomes backline-dive immunity. In the straight 1v1 his W damage-cut and silence cancel your burst while your ult cancels his peel, so neither of you cleanly wins. Make your early-to-mid pressure mean something on the map before it's just two bruisers trading even.","whys":["Garen edges level 1 — his Q silence cancels your axe wind-up and his passive regen heals any poke you land.","His level-2 empowered Q-strike plus W tenacity out-trades your Q-auto before your E combo is online.","At 3 his silence still shuts off your E true-damage nuke and his W tenacity ignores your Q-slow.","Through 4-5 his short W-cut trade and disengage beat your axe-reset pattern; hold E and wait for 6.","Level 6 flips to you — Ragnarok's immunity holds while you swing, so his silence stops nothing you throw.","First item returns the edge to him: Stridebreaker and W tenacity let him disengage your perma-slow again.","Late is genuinely even — his R execute and your dive immunity cancel out, neither wins the clean 1v1."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"graves","win":["Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Land your Q-axe to slow him, walk on top and auto — your passive attack speed ramps as you take his shotgun-auto poke, and he has no E-dash unlock yet to escape."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E's guaranteed true damage you can chunk him for free — bait his E-dash, then E when he can't reset distance."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep attacking, and Smoke Screen only cuts vision — perma-slow with axe resets and run him down."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His tanky-ADC build (Eclipse/Maw + bork) lets him burst-and-disengage with E-dash before you commit — force the fight before he gets there."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Undertow and stick on top — your missing-health attack speed and lifesteal win the extended trade","Bait Quickdraw's 16s dash, then Reckless Swing when he cannot reset the gap","Hit 6 and use Ragnarok's disable immunity to perma-slow him with axe resets and dive"],"foe":["Use his E-dash to reset auto distance and kite your Q-slow without ever standing still","Drop Smoke Screen to slow you and cut the vision you need to chase him","Stack True Grit resists off Quickdraw, chunk you, then disengage before Reckless Swing"]},"early":"Graves can't really kite you yet — Quickdraw is his only reset and at level 1 it isn't even unlocked, so land Undertow to slow him, walk on top, and let your attack speed ramp as his shotgun chips you. The catch is the resists: every Quickdraw toward you stacks True Grit, and Smoke Screen slows you and cuts your sight, so you lose him mid-chase. Bait the dash or the smoke, then commit — once those are down he has no answer to your speed.","mid":"This is your window. Undertow refunds on every pickup so you perma-slow him, Tough It Out shields the shotgun poke while your missing-health lifesteal heals it, and Reckless Swing's true damage cuts through the True Grit resists Quickdraw stacks. At 6, Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep swinging, and Smoke Screen only cuts your vision — it never stops an axe. Force the all-in on Quickdraw's 16s.","late":"You own lane and most of the mid-game, but Graves is the one window where a ranged carry can flip it late — his tanky build (Eclipse, Maw, bork) plus E-dash lets him burst you and dash out before you land your E, and his shotgun damage scales harder than your flat true damage. Your job is to be so far ahead from the early dives that it never matters. Convert your lead into towers and objectives, and don't try to walk him down 1v1 once he's 3+ items deep.","whys":["No E-dash unlocked at level 1, so Q-slow into autos sticks him and your passive ramps as his shotgun chips you — you win first contact.","His E-dash and smoke-blind come online and let him reset and kite your Q, but you can still bait-and-punish — genuinely even who gets the read first.","You have Q-slow plus E true damage to burst, but his E-dash plus True Grit poke can trade back if he kites clean — comes down to baiting his dash.","Your axe reset perma-slows him and missing-health lifesteal out-lasts his poke — Quickdraw cannot reset the gap fast enough.","Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you swing, and Smoke Screen only cuts your vision — it never stops an attack, so Reckless Swing finishes.","Your bruiser core (Bramble/Cleaver) plus axe-reset slows is your most oppressive point while his tanky build is still half-finished — dive him now.","You stay ahead of his item timing in this window — force the all-in before his Eclipse/Maw + E-dash lets him burst-and-disengage from late-game range."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"gwen","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Q-slow into auto wins first contact before her E-dash is up — chunk her on her first creep approach."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Axe-reset perma-slow and missing-health lifesteal out-last her Snip Snip! poke in short trades."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her W window: Hallowed Mist blocks everyone standing outside it, so she snips Snip Snip! from safety unless you walk in — her biggest swing at 6."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Gwen takes over: Riftmaker/Nashor stacked AP through Mist means your flat E true damage and short fights stop closing her out."}],"wants":{"you":["Force a Lvl 1-3 all-in: Q-slow sticks her, E true-damage burst before her W Mist is leveled","Bait out Skip 'n Slash and her Q poke, then heal the trade back and re-slow off the axe pickup","Convert your early lead into towers and objectives before she stacks 2+ AP items"],"foe":["Sit in Hallowed Mist so you must step inside to touch her while she snips away","Use E-dash for attack speed and spacing to kite your slow, never trading inside her Mist","Survive to 2+ items (Riftmaker, Nashor's) where her per-cent and true damage out-scales your flat kit"]},"early":"Gwen is a brutal level 1-3 for you to punish — her W Mist isn't online yet and her E-dash burns her only escape. Land Q to slow her, walk up, and E her for the guaranteed true-damage chunk; your passive attack speed ramps as you take her Q poke, so longer trades favour you. Pick your axe back up to refund Q and re-slow her if she tries to walk away. Just don't dump E when she still has E-dash and a wave to peel into.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are still yours: the axe reset perma-slows her and your missing-health lifesteal eats her Snip Snip! poke in any short fight, and she cannot kite a slowed target out of auto range yet. The lane flips at 6 — Hallowed Mist only stops enemies who stay outside it, so from range your axe finds nothing while she snips and heals. The answer is to step in, not to back off: walk into the mist and Reckless Swing her, or wait its 22s out.","late":"You built your whole game on the early lead, because late is hers. Stacked Riftmaker and Nashor's AP through the mist means Snip Snip!'s true damage and per-cent burst out-scale your flat kit. Your lifesteal cannot keep up with a fed Gwen, and she re-mists the moment you commit Ragnarok. Close the game on your timers — towers, dives, objectives — before her two items come online, or this becomes unwinnable.","whys":["Q-slow into auto wins first contact and Gwen's level 1 is weak with no Mist and E-dash as her only out.","Even Q-poke trade — her Q true damage answers your auto pressure before your E combo is fully online.","Skill window — your E true-damage burst trades with her Q poke; it comes down to who lands their spacing.","Your axe-reset perma-slow and missing-health lifesteal out-last her poke — she cannot kite a slowed target.","Hallowed Mist only blocks enemies outside it — step in and she is targetable again, but her Snip Snip! is free in there.","She Q-true-damages and heals from inside Mist; her first-item AP spike beats your bruiser core in extended fights.","Skill — she out-scales but you can still spike a kill on her cooldowns or end the game before her second item lands."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Olaf","Skill","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Before his turrets stack you can Q-slow and auto him off CS, your one clean uncontested window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes the grenade stun irrelevant while you keep swinging, but his turret nest still chunks you mid-dive."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Heimerdinger's Liandry's + Rylai turret upgrade (R) turns the wave into a no-go zone your bruiser core cannot tank through."},{"when":"Late","text":"Three upgraded turrets plus W rocket poke wall you off every objective; one missed E-grenade dodge is your only path in."}],"wants":{"you":["Hard-shove level 1 and crash before his turrets stack, then trade Q-slow into auto and E true-damage burst","Save Ragnarok's 100s for the grenade, then keep swinging so the stun never lands","Bait the E grenade, then Q-slow and E-nuke him in the gap before he can re-zone with a turret"],"foe":["Stack three turrets on the wave so you cannot walk up without taking tower-grade poke","Land the E stun-grenade to cancel your all-in before Ragnarok or save it for when R is down","Poke you with W rockets and turret beams while his minions and turret wall block your Q line"]},"early":"Level 1 is your only free moment — before he plants a second turret you can Q-slow him and auto him off a last-hit, so take that contact and crash the wave. The problem starts the instant his turret nest is up: it body-blocks your Q axe line, denies the slow-stick you live on, and chips you every time you walk up to CS. Do not facecheck into a stacked nest for a melee trade you cannot win, and respect his E stun-grenade — eating it level 2-3 means free turret-and-W damage with no Ragnarok to wash it off.","mid":"Levels 4-6 he settles in: Hextech Micro-Rockets poke you under your own tower and the turret wall keeps Undertow from ever sticking the slow. At 6 Ragnarok holds off his grenade stun as long as you keep attacking, so that is the one window you commit — Flash or walk in, Undertow, Tough It Out for the shield, and Reckless Swing him. The nest still chunks you on the way in, and if he holds the 11s grenade for after R ends you get walled right back out. Bring your jungler; alone you trade a health bar for one turret.","late":"This is where it slips fully out of reach. Three upgraded turrets plus Liandry's/Rylai rockets zone you off every objective, and Reckless Swing's flat true damage and your missing-health lifesteal stop mattering against a wall you cannot tank through. Your only path is baiting the grenade and flanking where his turrets are not set up, or letting your team pull the nest while you dive the carry behind it. Do not splitpush into his side lane — that is the chokepoint he is built to hold.","whys":["Before his turrets stack you out-stat him at melee — Q-slow into auto and your passive attack speed win the very first contact.","Once a second turret is up the nest body-blocks your Q line and pokes you off CS — neither of you cleanly owns this beat.","His E stun-grenade and W rockets punish every walk-up and you have no Ragnarok yet to wash off the turret damage.","The turret wall denies your Q-slow-stick all of levels 4-5, so your short-trade kit never gets to connect.","Ragnarok's immunity holds off the grenade while you swing, but the turret nest still chunks the dive and he can wait R out.","His Liandry's + Rylai turret upgrade (R) turns the wave into a no-go zone your Black Cleaver bruiser core cannot push through.","Three upgraded turrets plus W rocket poke wall you off every objective while your flat true damage falls off — he scales past you."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"illaoi","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi","Illaoi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Q-slow into autos wins first contact before she has a tentacle field — your one clean early window."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Her E (Test of Spirit) plus a tentacle wall flips trades — if she rips your spirit you must run from your own tentacles and she heals off the slam."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok holds off her CC while you keep attacking — 100s, so spend it to all-in or dive her off her field."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her tentacle stacks plus sustain reclaim lane — her field out-heals your lifesteal in any extended brawl."}],"wants":{"you":["Win Level 1 with Q-slow-into-auto before any tentacles exist on the wave","Use Ragnarok at 6 to ignore her E and tentacle-field CC and dive her","Fight in the open river/lane edges, never inside her stacked tentacle field"],"foe":["Land E (Test of Spirit) to rip your spirit so her tentacles chunk and heal her","Stack tentacles around her so every trade happens inside her healing field","Bait your E (Reckless Swing) self-damage, then slam you with a full field"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: throw Q for the slow and walk an auto in before she has a single tentacle planted, because a fieldless Illaoi has no answer to a stuck axe. But the moment she has E up this flips — do NOT facetank a trade next to her tentacles, and never let her land Test of Spirit on you, or you spend the trade running from your own spirit-vessel while her tentacles slam and heal her. Last-hit at Q range, pick the axe back up to chain slows, and refuse the extended brawl she wants.","mid":"Levels 3-5 belong to her: every tentacle heals her when it connects, so her field out-lasts your lifesteal, and Reckless Swing costs you health she punishes instantly. Don't burn it here — farm and respect Test of Spirit's 16s. Remember Harsh Lesson leaps her back onto you every 4 seconds, so there is no walking a fight off inside her field. Level 6 is your one reclaim window: Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune as long as you keep attacking, so that is when you all-in or tower-dive her — off her tentacles she is immobile.","late":"This is her game. At first item her tentacle stacks and AOE healing turn every extended fight into a loss, and your flat true damage plus short-fight kit can't out-trade a stacked field. Your only path is to convert any Level 1 or Level 6 lead into objectives and dives before her tentacles snowball — pull her off her field in teamfights with Ragnarok and kill her fast, because standing in her zone is death.","whys":["Level 1 a fieldless Illaoi has no tentacles, so your Q-slow-into-auto wins first contact outright.","Once Test of Spirit is up the trade evens — she rips your spirit, but Undertow's slow and your shield still hold.","Her tentacle stacks and the healing off them out-last your lifesteal, and punish every Reckless Swing you throw.","Levels 4-5 she has a real field up — Test of Spirit plus tentacle slams beat your short trades and heal it all back.","Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep swinging in her field — this is your all-in and dive window.","At first item her tentacle stacks and AOE healing reclaim the lane — her field out-heals anything you can dish out.","At 2+ items it is a knife-edge: you must pull her off her tentacles and burst her, or her stacked field wins the brawl."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"irelia","win":["Olaf","Skill","Irelia","Irelia","Skill","Irelia","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"You win first contact — Q-slow into autos chunks her before her Q has minion targets to dash-reset off, so she can't kite the opener."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune as long as you keep attacking, so her stun stops peeling and a fed Irelia gets run down instead."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Her threat window: she stacks her passive on you, Q-dashes through minions to reset trades, and E-stuns the second you walk up to throw Q."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Your axe-and-true-damage kit goes flat while her item spikes turn extended fights in her favor — close before she three-items."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level-1 Q-slow opener before she has minions to Q-dash off and reset","Land Reckless Swing in short bursts — Defiant Dance only cuts physical damage, never true","Hit 6 and hold Ragnarok for her stun, then keep swinging so it never lands"],"foe":["Use Q to dash through minions and reset every trade so your axe-slow never sticks","Land her E-stun the instant you step up to throw Q, then stack her passive on you","Charge Defiant Dance to cut your physical damage and drag the fight long to out-scale"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours — throw Q to slow her, walk up and auto, and your passive attack speed ramps as you take her return hits; she has no minions yet to Q-dash off so she can't reset the trade. The danger starts the moment minions arrive: her Q dashes through them to reset and her E stuns you the instant you wind up another Q. Don't throw Q from inside her E range, and pick your axe back up to keep the cooldown low so you always have a slow ready when she dashes in.","mid":"This is her window and you have to respect it. From 3 to 5 she stacks her passive on your autos and Bladesurges through the wave, healing on every reset, so a long trade favors her — keep them short and let your missing-health lifesteal top you off. Defiant Dance only cuts PHYSICAL damage, so Reckless Swing lands through it in full. Everything flips at 6: Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep attacking, so her stun cannot peel. Bait the E or wait it out, then ult and commit.","late":"The math turns on her at items but not in your favor — your flat Reckless Swing true damage and short axe fights lose value while her item spikes make every extended duel hers, and Bladesurge heals back what you chip. You don't out-scale her, so don't try to win this lane at three items. Convert the level-6 Ragnarok dives and your early pressure into towers and objectives, then become the diver who ults past her peel onto their backline instead of duelling a scaled Irelia.","whys":["You win first contact — Q-slows her and your passive ramps attack speed before she has minions to Q-dash off and reset.","Trades are even now: your axe-slow and her Q-reset cancel out, and neither of you can commit a clean kill without burning a key cooldown.","She stacks her passive and Q-resets through the wave faster than your axe pickup refunds, edging the level-3 short trade.","Flawless Duet stuns your wind-up and Bladesurge heals her on every reset, so she controls the 4-5 window.","Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep swinging, so her stun cannot peel and your true damage evens the all-in.","Her first-item spike powers the extended fight her W and resets want, while your flat true damage hasn't scaled — she reclaims this stage.","Past her peel you ult onto her with Ragnarok's CC-immunity and run her down before her items fully matter — your last clean window."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"jax","win":["Olaf","Jax","Jax","Skill","Olaf","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"First contact is yours — Q-slow into autos and your passive attack speed ramping as you take damage beat Jax before he has Q or E."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Jax's danger window — once he has Q-leap plus E Counter Strike he can dodge your Q, stun your autos, and burst you on the W-Q-E combo."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok gives passive resists and disable immunity while you keep swinging — dive him now, before his items land."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Jax reclaims the duel with Trinity Force plus Sterak's: his E dodges your autos and his ramping on-hits out-DPS your flat true damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Win first contact at Level 1 with Q-slow into autos before Jax has his Q-leap or E","All-in at 6: keep swinging under Ragnarok so his stun never lands, and slow him","Convert your early lead into plates, dives and objectives before his 2-item Trinity spike"],"foe":["Reach Level 2-3 so he has Q-leap and E Counter Strike to dodge your Q and stun your autos","Bait your all-in onto active E so its dodge-and-stun blanks your trade","Stall to two items where Trinity Force and Sterak's ramping out-scales your flat true damage"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours — lead with Q to slow him, walk up, and let Berserker Rage ramp your attack speed as he chips you; he has no leap and no Counter Strike yet, so he can't dodge or stun. The danger starts at 2-3: once Jax has Q-leap and E up, do NOT auto into an active E — the dodge eats your autos and the stun flips the trade. Throw Q to keep him slowed so he can't gap-close cleanly, pick the axe back up to refund it, and only commit E true damage when his E is down.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a knife-fight: respect Counter Strike's 17s above all else — bait it by faking the all-in, then commit once it is down and your missing-health lifesteal out-grinds him. Six is your spike: Ragnarok's resists plus disable immunity while you keep attacking let you dive through his combo and stick him with Undertow while your attack speed ramps. This is the window for plates or a kill — his Trinity Force isn't online yet.","late":"This is where Jax takes the lane back. Once Trinity Force and Sterak's come online his E dodges your autos, his W-empowered on-hits ramp, and his R defensive stats let him out-trade your flat E true damage in any extended fight. Your kit is a short-fight, early-bully kit — don't sit and scale into him. Use your level 6 lead to snowball side lanes, dive squishier targets with Ragnarok in teamfights, and end before his two-item spike makes the straight duel his.","whys":["You own first contact — Q-slow into autos plus your passive attack speed ramping beat a Jax who has no leap or E Counter Strike yet.","Jax hits his power spike — with Q-leap and E up he dodges your Q approach, stuns your autos, and bursts you on W-Q-E.","He keeps the edge at 3 — his E dodge-and-stun blanks your committed trade while his Q gap-close resets distance you can't punish.","Genuinely even — a pure Counter Strike timing duel: bait its 17s and your missing-health lifesteal wins the grind, eat the stun and you lose.","Ragnarok's passive resists plus disable immunity while you swing let you dive his combo and stick the slow — your strongest window.","Still a coin-flip — your bruiser-core lane pressure is real but Jax's first Trinity component starts closing the duel gap.","Even on paper but trending his way — your flat E true damage plateaus while Jax's Trinity plus Sterak's ramping on-hits and R reclaim the duel."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Jayce","Skill","Jayce"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Jayce's cannon-form Q acceleration gate and E knockback poke you before you ever reach Q-throw range — his strongest window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok holds his disables off while you keep swinging, so you walk through the poke and force the melee all-in he cannot answer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble plus missing-health lifesteal makes your all-in oppressive — chain axe slows and he can't kite out."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past two items Jayce's burst combo and range start chunking you before you commit — close the game before this window."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit 6 and keep swinging under Ragnarok so his disables never land on the all-in","Land Q to perma-slow him so his stance-swap kiting can't create distance","Let the missing-health passive heal his poke back, and end the lane by two items"],"foe":["Poke you down with cannon-Q acceleration gate before you close range","Use E knockback to interrupt your all-in and reset to ranged stance","Stall the lane with range so his burst combo outscales you at two items"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 belong to Jayce — his cannon-form Q fires through the acceleration gate for huge ranged poke, and his E knockback shoves you off any approach before your Q-axe even lands. Don't walk straight at him to throw Q; he'll just gate-poke you and knock you back. Soak XP at the edge of his range, pick up your axe to refund the cooldown, and chip his health from max throw distance. Accept that you're behind on this trade pattern until you spike.","mid":"Levels 4-5 even out as your missing-health lifesteal and axe-reset slows let you survive his poke and start sticking to him. Then Level 6 flips the lane hard: Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune as long as you keep attacking, so Thundering Blow stops peeling and you force the melee all-in. Undertow to perma-slow, Reckless Swing to his face, and your attack speed ramps as his poke lands. He has no answer once you're on top of him.","late":"Your first-item bruiser spike (Black Cleaver, Bramble, missing-health lifesteal) is your most oppressive point — every all-in heals you up and his burst can't trade with that. But past two items Jayce reclaims the matchup: his range and full burst combo chunk you before you commit, and your flat true damage stops scaling. Convert the early-to-mid lead into towers, dives and objectives — never a poke war at three items.","whys":["His cannon-Q acceleration gate out-ranges everything you have at Level 1 — you can only soak XP and last-hit at axe range.","With E knockback online he interrupts any step-up and pokes you for free before your Q can land.","His full poke kit chunks you each time you approach; pick your axe back up and farm rather than force a trade you lose.","Your missing-health lifesteal and axe-reset slows let you survive and stick — the lane levels as you close.","Ragnarok keeps you disable-immune while you keep swinging, so his poke can't peel and Reckless Swing finishes it.","Black Cleaver / Bramble plus missing-health lifesteal makes the all-in unbeatable — chain axe slows and he can't escape.","You still beat him in melee, but force every fight now before his two-item burst and range outscale your flat true damage."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Karma","Karma","Olaf","Karma","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Karma's Q (Inner Flame) outranges you and she E-shields the cone, so her early poke chunks you before your axe lands."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok cleanses her RQ root and tether the instant she casts it, letting you walk through the snare and E her face for true damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her Mandate/Lost Chapter spike lets her perma-shield and kite; only commit when her E shield is already on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Pick up every thrown axe to refund Q and chain the slow, or her E move-speed simply walks her out of your all-in."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her E shield + RQ root, then ult to ignore the snare and E her down","Catch the Q-slow on her so she can't kite, then close with passive attack speed","Pick the axe back up to refund Q and re-slow before her E move-speed resets the gap"],"foe":["Poke with Q (Inner Flame) from max range and shield the return with E","Land RQ root + tether to peel your all-in before your Ragnarok is up","Use E move-speed to kite back the second you commit and out-sustain with shields"]},"early":"Karma owns the first few levels because her Q (Inner Flame) outranges your axe and her E shields whatever you trade back. Don't chase a Q throw into her — she'll just E-walk away and poke you on the return. Last-hit at the edge of your Q-slow range, eat minimal poke, and respect that her shield turns your guaranteed E true-damage hit into a non-kill. Your sustain from W omnivamp is your lifeline here, not your trades.","mid":"Levels 4-5 still belong to her poke-and-shield pattern, but 6 is your window — Ragnarok removes and immunizes you to her RQ root AND tether, so bait the snare, ult through it, and run her down while your passive attack speed ramps. Land Q first so she can't E-kite, then E her face. This is the one clean all-in you get before her items, so do not waste your ult clearing a wave.","late":"Once Karma hits her Lost Chapter / Mandate spike she perma-shields and her E move-speed kites you out of every commit, so the lane flattens to even — you trade dives for her poke. Your edge is the axe-reset: pick up every Undertow to refund Q and keep the slow glued on her, because the moment she's free of it her E walks her out of true-damage range. Force objectives on your Ragnarok timer; don't wait for a scaling game that favors her shields.","whys":["Her Q (Inner Flame) outranges your axe and she E-shields the trade, so she pokes you for free at level 1.","She still poke-shields at 2 and your Q-slow can't stick through her E move-speed.","With RQ-tether unlocked at 3 she roots-and-kites any step-up before your sustain matters.","Levels 4-5 she perma-shields short trades and your E nuke just gets absorbed.","Ragnarok cleanses her RQ root and tether — you walk through the snare and E her down before she resets.","Her first-item shield uptime returns and her E move-speed kites you off every all-in.","At 2+ items it's even: you chain axe-slows to dive, she shields and E-kites — skill decides each fight."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"kassadin","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks a Kassadin who has nothing but his magic shield and a single Q to answer you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Kassadin's R lets him blink away the instant you commit, so your axe-slow stops sticking and your all-in whiffs."},{"when":"1st item","text":"He stacks Rod of Ages / Tear and rolling R-passive haste — every blink costs less and he kites your slows clean."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-build Kassadin blinks in on a 2s Riftwalk and bursts you down before your true damage ever matters."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q axes and pick them up to perma-slow him so he can't walk to CS","Force E true-damage trades before 6 while his only defense is the Q shield","Snowball levels 1-5 and crash waves to deny him farm before R online"],"foe":["Survive to 6 and use R blinks to dodge your Q and reset every trade","Blink out with Riftwalk the moment you E in so your true-damage burst whiffs","Hit Rod of Ages / Catalyst stacks and roll R cooldown to scale past you"]},"early":"Kassadin is one of the worst level-1-to-5 champs in the game and you are one of the best, so press it hard. Null Sphere leaves him a magic-damage shield and Void Stone cuts magic damage — but you deal physical and true, so neither blunts your trade. Throw Q to slow, walk up, and land E for guaranteed true damage; pick the axe back up to refund it and keep him perma-slowed off CS. Null Sphere only interrupts channels, so nothing he has stops your combo — walk him down.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you still win every short trade — W omnivamp heals back his Q poke and your slows mean he can't walk away. But 6 flips the lane: Ragnarok gives YOU CC immunity, yet Kassadin's R is a blink, not CC, so he just teleports out of your axe-slow and resets. From here your all-in stops landing cleanly. Crash waves and roam or take plates while he's still weak — every minute you stall him from items is a minute he can't blink-kite you.","late":"This is all Kassadin. Once he has Rod of Ages and Riftwalk sits at its 2s rank-3 cooldown, he blinks in, blinks straight back out of your reach, and bursts you before your flat true damage adds up. You cannot catch a champion whose whole kit is repeatable blinks. Your only path is to have already ended it — convert your level 1-6 lead into towers, dives and a gold gap so his scaling never gets to matter. If it goes 25+ minutes even, you lose.","whys":["Kassadin is a famously weak level 1 and your Q-slow-into-auto plus passive attack speed win first contact outright.","At 2 your Q+E gives a guaranteed true-damage burst his magic shield can't absorb and he has no escape yet.","Level 3 you out-trade hard — axe-reset slows keep him pinned while W omnivamp heals his only counter, Q poke.","Even window: you still win the short trade, but he's now close enough to 6 that he plays for the R blink, not the duel.","Ragnarok gives you CC immunity but his R is a blink, not CC — he teleports out of your slow and your all-in whiffs.","His first-item Rod of Ages / Tear and dropping R cooldown let him kite your axes and reset trades you used to win.","Full-build Kassadin blinks every 2s on Riftwalk and bursts you before flat true damage matters — he scales clean past you."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"kayle","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Kayle","Kayle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow into E's true-damage nuke you can chunk a defenseless early Kayle for nearly half her bar before she has any range to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok ignores any peel and Berserker Rage's missing-health lifesteal carries the long trade — your last clean all-in before her invuln R."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Kayle hits Nashor's/Berserker's her ranged form kites your Q and her R invulnerability negates your E burst — the lane flips here."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-build Kayle waveclears, kites and R-invulns through your all-in; you cannot duel her, so this window belongs to her."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow then E true-damage nuke every time she steps up to last-hit, stacking a level lead before 6","Use Tough It Out's attack speed and Berserker Rage lifesteal to win the long melee trade","Snowball levels 1-5 and convert it into dives/objectives before her ranged form and R come online"],"foe":["Survive to ranged form and her first item where she kites your Q and out-DPS's your trades","Bait your E and R then R-invuln through the all-in to deny your kill","Farm safe under tower, scale to Nashor's/full-build and take over the late game"]},"early":"Kayle is melee, slow, and one of the weakest level-1s in the game right now — and you are the opposite. Lead with Q to slow her off a CS, then walk up and E her face for guaranteed true damage; she has no dash, no range, and no answer to your passive ramping attack speed as you trade. Chain your axe pickups to keep the slow on her so she can never walk away, and look to deny last-hits to choke her XP. Every level you keep her behind here is a level she stays melee.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your conversion window — keep using axe-reset slows and W sustain to win short trades, and at 6 your Ragnarok lets you ignore any flash/peel attempt and run her down with E. She gets no invulnerable R yet, so this is the moment to all-in or set up a dive with your jungler. Be honest though: if she's farmed safe and you can't land the slow, she's about to hit ranged form, so force the kill NOW rather than letting her cross into her first item.","late":"This is Kayle's game and you know it. Once she's at Nashor's and beyond, her ranged autos kite your Q from outside E range, her waveclear erases your wave pressure, and her R invulnerability simply turns off your entire all-in mid-combo. You do not win this duel — don't try. Use your early lead to take towers, herald and grubs, group with your team, and dive whatever she's not standing next to; your only path is ending before her scaling fully arrives.","whys":["Kayle is among the weakest level-1s and is melee with no escape — your Q-slow-into-auto wins first contact outright.","Your Q plus E gives a guaranteed true-damage burst she has zero range to trade back against.","Axe-reset slows pin her in place while E chunks her — a defenseless melee Kayle can't survive your short trades.","She's still melee and you out-sustain with W, but she's farming toward ranged form so the window is closing — genuinely even now.","Ragnarok ignores her peel and Berserker Rage lifesteals harder as you drop, but Divine Judgment saves her — a coin-flip on execution.","Once she hits ranged form and her first item she kites your Q and her R invulnerability negates your E — the lane flips to her.","Full-build Kayle out-ranges, waveclears and R-invulns through everything you do — accept you lose the duel and play the map."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"kennen","win":["Skill","Kennen","Skill","Olaf","Kennen","Skill","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Land Q to slow Kennen the second he steps for a CS, walk on top of him and trade an auto — your only clean window before his energy poke starts ticking."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok blanks Mark of the Storm while you keep swinging — pop it as Slicing Maelstrom lands, then E his face for true damage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble online: Q-reset perma-slow plus Berserker Rage lifesteal walks him down through every Q/W poke he lands."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Kennen's peak poke window — before you can hard-engage he chips you with double Q shurikens and W mark procs from max range."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to perma-slow Kennen and close the gap before his energy poke adds up","Bait his R, then Ragnarok through the stun and E him down with true damage","Force the all-in at 6 and first item before he gets kite range and zhonyas"],"foe":["Poke you with Q shuriken and W mark procs from max range on his energy economy","Keep move speed and distance so your Q never sticks and your E never reaches","Land his R stun on your engage to kite back and chunk you before you commit"]},"early":"Kennen has no escape and dies if you ever touch him, so the early game is all about landing Q. Hit the axe through him as he steps up for a CS, then walk on top while the slow holds and trade an auto — at Level 1 you win that exchange easily. The catch is his energy poke: from 2-3 he chips you with double Q shurikens and W mark procs that you can't punish from range, so don't sit in shuriken range farming. Pick up your thrown axe to refund the cooldown and keep the slow ready for the next step-up.","mid":"This is where you take over. Berserker Rage lifesteals back everything his Q/W poke does, and a Q-reset perma-slow means once you're on him he can't kite out. The whole lane pivots on Slicing Maelstrom: he wants the triple-mark stun the instant you engage so he can dance away. So bait it — its 120s is your window — or pop Ragnarok as the stun lands so it never holds you, then E his face. A Kennen with no ult and no flash is dead.","late":"You owned this lane, but Kennen scales into an AOE teamfight ult that doesn't care how hard you beat him 1v1. Your flat true damage and short-fight kit lose value the moment he has Zhonyas and full AP. Don't let it get there: convert your early-mid kill pressure into plates, your jungler's ganks, and Herald, and make his lane irrelevant before his ult swings fights. Late, respect his R flash-engage onto your carries and use Ragnarok to dive HIM, not to chase a kited fight you can't win.","whys":["Kennen has no escape but outranges you — Level 1 goes to whoever lands first, your axe or his shuriken.","Level 2-3 is his poke peak: double Q shurikens plus W mark procs chip you from a range you can't yet punish.","With Q-slow plus E true damage you can answer his poke, but his shuriken chip keeps it a coin-flip on who's healthier.","Berserker Rage lifesteals harder the lower you drop, and the Q-reset slow lets you stick and trade short — you out-grind him.","Without R up he can't peel, but the moment he lands his AOE stun on your step-up he kites you and his level-6 spike edges it.","Your first item lets you perma-slow and walk him down, but Slicing Maelstrom is back every 120s — it stays a read.","His teamfight ult and Zhonyas matter late, but in the straight lane you still dive him with Ragnarok and E him through it."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"kled","win":["Olaf","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kled","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"You out-stat him at first contact — land Undertow then auto while the slow sticks, before his mounted Q-grab range comes online."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Kled's spike: with Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) plus Violent Tendencies (W) he pulls you in and shreds your low armor faster than your E true damage can answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Skaarl charges in with Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) — if you stand to fight him you eat the dismount knockback and his remount burst; sidestep the charge line."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Even window — your bruiser core trades into his, but his remount full-HP reset means you must kill him before he dismounts to scale past you."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level-1 first contact: Undertow slow into autos before his Bear Trap (Q) range and dismount aggression come online","Bait Skaarl's dismount, then Reckless Swing true damage and Berserker Rage lifesteal through his unmounted state","Snowball the early lead into towers and objectives before his remount resets carry him to scale"],"foe":["Land Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) to pull you in and reset trades while his W shreds your armor","Bait your E and all-in commit, then survive to dismount and remount for a full-HP reset","Use Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) to engage or escape and out-scale you once Skaarl is back"]},"early":"Level 1 is genuinely yours — throw Undertow (Q), let the slow stick, and auto him before his mounted Bear Trap (Q) grab range turns the corner aggression in his favor. The problem starts at 2-3: once Kled has his Q-pull plus Violent Tendencies (W) attack-speed steroid, he yanks you in and his autos rip through your low early armor faster than your E true-damage nuke heals back through W. Don't walk up to throw a Q into his pull range — poke with the tail of Undertow and pick the axe back up to keep the cooldown low, but respect that he wins the extended trade he forces.","mid":"Through 4-5 he stays ahead — his dismount-state damage and remount reset mean even when you chunk him with Reckless Swing, he survives to remount at full HP and wins the rematch. At 6 his Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) lets Skaarl barrel into you with a knockback on contact; Ragnarok has to be up BEFORE that, since it blanks disables only while you keep swinging and does nothing about the raw burst. Your one real path: bait his dismount with a short fight, then collapse the unmounted Kled on Berserker Rage lifesteal before he remounts.","late":"By 2+ items it levels off into a coin-flip — your Black Cleaver / bruiser core trades into his, and Ragnarok still lets you ignore his peel to dive. But Kled is the harder scaler here: his remount is a free full-HP reset every fight, so a drawn-out brawl favors him. Your flat E true damage stops carrying the way it did at level 2, so convert any early-mid edge into towers and objectives — if the game goes long and even, his reset out-grinds your short-fight kit.","whys":["You own first contact: Undertow's slow into an auto wins level 1 before his Bear Trap (Q) range and dismount aggression are online.","His spike arrives — Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) pulls you in and Violent Tendencies (W) shreds your low armor faster than E can answer.","His remount mechanic means even a clean E-Reckless-Swing only chunks him; he survives to reset and wins the rematch.","He keeps edging short trades — his dismount burst plus a full-HP remount out-grinds Berserker Rage lifesteal.","Chaaaaaaaarge!!! (R) knocks you back and bursts on remount; Ragnarok blanks the CC while you keep swinging, not the damage.","His first bruiser item plus the remount reset stays ahead of your flat E true damage in the extended brawl.","Roughly even — your bruiser core dives through his peel with Ragnarok, but his remount reset out-scales a long game, so close it earlier."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"ksante","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Q-slow into autos wins first contact — K'Sante has no W block charged and no dash to escape the chase yet."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q+E or Q+W comes online — your guaranteed E true damage chunks him before his percent-HP passive matters."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok blanks Path Maker's stun while you keep swinging, so the one combo he has to stop your dive does nothing — E him down."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His biggest window: with a Heartsteel/tank core his W blocks your E and his All Out form duels you back as your flat true damage stops scaling."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to perma-slow him so he can never walk out of your E true-damage range","Force short all-ins at 2-6 where Berserker Rage's missing-health lifesteal out-sustains his percent-HP tankiness","Press Ragnarok through Path Maker's stun and blow up his trade before his items land"],"foe":["Block your E nuke and your Q axe with W (Path Maker) to deny your whole combo","Bait Ragnarok with his dash, then peel back with Q knockup once it expires","Stall to 2+ items where his All Out R form and tank stats let him duel you back"]},"early":"Q him on cooldown — the axe slow is the whole lane, because once it sticks he cannot walk out of your E range, and E's guaranteed true damage cuts straight through his percent-HP passive that normally shrugs off bruisers. Level 1 is yours: he has no W block charged and no way to escape the slow. The only thing to respect is his W (Path Maker) — it can dash through and block one of your axes or your E, so do not throw E into a fully-charged W. Pick your axe back up to refund the cooldown and chain-slow him for the next trade.","mid":"From 4-5 he edges it — he holds Path Maker to eat your E and the Ntofo pull at 2 stacks drags you off the chase, while Berserker Rage lifesteals back what you can. At 6 Ragnarok is the answer: it blanks Path Maker's stun for as long as you keep swinging, so the one combo he has to stop a dive does nothing. Bait the W dash out first, then all-in — but he can do the same to your ult, dashing away to run the 100s down before re-engaging.","late":"This is his game, not yours. K'Sante is a hard scaler — once he hits 2+ items his W blocks your E nuke, his tank stats and percent-HP passive eat your flat true damage, and his All Out R form lets him strip his own resists and duel you straight up while you have stopped scaling. Your job is to never let it get here: convert your level-1-to-6 lead into plates, dives and grubs/herald, and roam with your tempo. If the game goes long, group and let your team peel him — do not 1v1 a full-build K'Sante.","whys":["You win first contact — Q-slow into autos lands free damage and he has no W charge or dash to escape it yet.","He gets W (Path Maker) to block an axe and his Q knockup to interrupt your step-up, so first blood goes to whoever lands their combo cleanly.","His percent-HP passive and W block start to neutralize your short trades, and his Q knockup buys him the disengage he needs.","He can hold W to eat your E nuke and use Q to peel every all-in, turning your slow-and-burst pattern into a stalemate as he edges toward items.","Ragnarok blanks Path Maker's stun and the Ntofo pull while you swing, but he can dash off with W and waste it — a coinflip on who commits.","Your bruiser core stays strong but his first tank item plus All Out R let him survive the burst, so the lane sits even.","At two items it is still even, but he is the one scaling — W blocks your E, tank stats eat your flat true damage, and All Out reclaims the duel from here."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"lillia","win":["Olaf","Skill","Skill","Lillia","Skill","Lillia","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"You win first contact: Q-slow into autos lands free damage before her passive DOT and W bounce can kite you off."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok blanks Lilting Lullaby while you keep swinging — and her sleep only lands on targets already carrying Dream Dust."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Her threat window: with Blooming Blows stacking move speed and Swirlseed slowing, she kites every Q you miss and DOTs you down."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"She out-skirmishes a flat-true-damage Olaf in extended fights — Liandry/Riftmaker DOT plus Blooming Blows' move speed beat your combos."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow so she can't kite, then close with Reckless Swing before her move speed stacks","Hit your Level 1-3 windows and snowball short trades before her W/E kite is online","Press Ragnarok before her sleep lands and force the all-in she cannot kite away from"],"foe":["Stack Blooming Blows move speed and Swirlseed slows to kite your Q misses and DOT you down","Land Dream Dust first, then Lilting Lullaby's sleep while your Ragnarok is down","Stall to 2+ items where her Liandry/Riftmaker DOT out-skirmishes your flat true damage"]},"early":"Lillia is an off-meta kiter up top, and the early game is yours. At Level 1 your Q-slow into autos beats her first contact — she has no point-blank trade, only passive DOT and Watch Out! Eep! on 14s. Throw Q to stick the slow, then walk her down before her move-speed stacks build. Pick your axe back up to keep the slow chained. Don't chase her into her own minions where Swirlseed rolls back into you; make her come to the wave and punish every step into range.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are her window: with Watch Out! Eep! and Swirlseed leveled she kites your Q misses, DOTs you with passive, and refuses the melee trade you need. If your axe whiffs, don't dry-chase — every spell she lands stacks her move speed further. Wait for 6: Ragnarok blanks Lilting Lullaby for as long as you keep swinging, and her sleep only takes on targets already carrying Dream Dust. Burn it on her commit, then Reckless Swing her down.","late":"This evens out and then slips. From 2+ items a Liandry/Riftmaker Lillia out-skirmishes flat-true-damage Olaf — her DOT and stacked move speed win the extended fight your short combo can't close. Your job is to have already converted the early lead into plates, dives, and objectives. In teamfights you can still Ragnarok-dive her backline, but the clean 1v1 tilts to her once her items come online. Don't let this go to a coinflip skirmish at three items.","whys":["Your Q-slow into auto wins first contact — she has no point-blank trade, only DOT and a W bounce that hasn't ramped yet.","Even race: your E true-damage threat is real but her passive DOT and W bounce let her trade back and kite the follow-up.","Skill window — land Q and you stick her for an E nuke; whiff it and she bounces out and DOTs you even.","Her spike: Blooming Blows stacks move speed and Swirlseed slows, so she kites every Q you miss and DOTs you.","Ragnarok cleanses her R sleep and W/E slows, turning a lane she normally kites into a committed all-in you win.","She edges it back — with W and E up and her R threat live, she resets every trade your axe doesn't lock down.","She out-skirmishes flat-true-damage Olaf at items: Liandry/Riftmaker DOT plus perma move-speed beats your short combos, so it's a coinflip you should have ended."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"lucian","win":["Lucian","Lucian","Lucian","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Lucian's level 2-3 double-Q + passive double-tap chunks you before you can land a Q-slow and walk in for E true damage."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's armour and MR blunt the Culling and its disable immunity beats any gank CC — this is your hardest all-in window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble online: your Q-slow sticks long enough to chase through his Culling and the omnivamp out-heals his poke."},{"when":"Late","text":"He never fully out-scales you the way a Vayne does, but if he gets 2+ items uncontested his Culling + E-resets kite your flat true damage — dive him before that."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q on him to lock the slow, then walk in for E's guaranteed true-damage chunk before he can E-dash out","Hold Ragnarok for the gank CC — its armour and MR also blunt his Culling burst","Use Berserker Rage lifesteal to heal back his double-tap poke and win short trades"],"foe":["Use his E-dash to dodge your Q and reset spacing before you reach E range","Double-tap you with passive + Q poke at range while you have no slow stuck","Save E to escape your Ragnarok dive and kite back with Culling"]},"early":"Lucian owns the first few levels here — his passive double-tap and double-Q poke chunk you at range before you ever stick a slow. Do not walk up to throw Q if it whiffs, because he just E-dashes the axe and double-taps you for free. Last-hit at max Q range, pick the axe back up to keep it on cooldown, and only commit when your Q actually lands the slow so you can close for E. Eat a little poke; your W omnivamp pays it back the moment you get a real trade.","mid":"This is where it flips to you. Once you have Q plus E your all-in beats his — land the axe, the slow sticks, you walk in and E's true damage ignores his lack of resistances. At 6, be clear about what Ragnarok does: he has no slow to cleanse and it grants no speed. What it gives you is armour and MR to eat a Culling and immunity to any disable while you keep swinging. Bait his E — 16s at rank 1 — then commit.","late":"Lucian is not a hard-scaler like Vayne, so you keep real agency all game — your Q-slow plus Black Cleaver lets you chase through his Culling, and W omnivamp out-sustains his poke in any extended fight. The danger is only if you let him farm uncontested to 2+ items, where his Culling and E-resets start kiting your flat true damage. Convert your level 6 and first-item windows into dives, plates, and skirmishes so the game never gets to the point where he can space you out.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s — his double-tap pokes but he can't commit, and your Q-slow-into-auto trades back evenly before either of you has a kill threat.","At 2 he gets double-Q plus passive double-tap and out-pokes you hard since your Q-slow alone can't force a winning trade yet.","Level 3 stays his — he can double-tap then E-dash out before your E true damage comes online, chunking you on the back foot.","With Q plus E your all-in beats his: land the slow, walk in, and E's guaranteed true damage cuts him down before he resets spacing.","Lucian has no slow at all, so Ragnarok's real gift is the passive armour and MR — at 6 you can eat a full Culling and still close for Reckless Swing.","Black Cleaver and Bramble online: your Q-slow sticks through his Culling and Berserker Rage out-heals his poke at your most oppressive point.","Unlike a true hypercarry he never fully escapes you — your Q-slow plus omnivamp keep you in the fight, so close it before his 2-item Culling-and-E kite takes over."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"malphite","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into a guaranteed E true-damage hit chunks him — but break Granite Shield first, or the first 10% of his max HP is simply free."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Malphite's R unstoppable knock-up is his one window to flip a trade he is losing, so this is the level you must respect his all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver shred plus E true damage and your perma-slow make Malphite's stacked armor nearly worthless in the 1v1."},{"when":"Late","text":"Malphite's teamfight R becomes a game-swinger, so close the lane and snowball before his armor and engage outvalue your flat true damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to slow Malphite, then E his face for guaranteed true damage his armor cannot reduce","Poke Granite Shield off before you commit — it soaks 10% of his max HP for free","Bait or wait out his level-6 R, then all-in while it is on cooldown"],"foe":["Poke you with Q on cooldown and farm safe under tower behind W armor","Chip you with Ground Slam every 7s so your attack speed and lifesteal never ramp","Stall the lane to 2+ items and matter as a teamfight engage rather than a duelist"]},"early":"Malphite has no kill pressure on you levels 1-3, but don't treat Seismic Shard as rare — it is a flat 8s at every rank and it steals your move speed as it slows. Land your Q to stick him, walk in for the E true-damage nuke, and chip Granite Shield off first so its 10% max-HP layer isn't eating your opener. Watch Ground Slam: 7s, and it cuts the attack speed your damage and lifesteal both run on.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep out-trading him with axe-reset slows, but Ground Slam every 7s keeps shaving the attack speed your damage rides on, so favour short bursts over long grinds. At 6 his 130s knock-up flips a trade he is otherwise losing — the answer is to already be in Ragnarok when he presses it, not to press yours afterwards. Once Black Cleaver lands his stacked armour is shredded and your E ignores it outright.","late":"You win every straight 1v1 against Malphite all game, but the danger is the map: his R is a teamfight-starting engage that lets him matter even when he loses lane. Don't let the game drag to 2+ items where his armor and AoE flip become more valuable than your flat true damage. Snowball your early lead into towers, dives, and objectives, and force fights before he can just sit in the back and ult your carry.","whys":["His Q is a single long-cooldown slow with no kill threat, while your Q-slow-into-auto and ramping passive win first contact outright.","Your Q plus E gives a guaranteed true-damage burst his armor cannot reduce and his Q poke cannot match.","Axe-reset slows stick him for repeated E hits, but Ground Slam's 7s attack-speed cut caps your ramp.","You stay favored chaining short trades, but his R unstoppable is now one button away, so it is genuinely even on his commit.","His 130s knock-up flips a trade he is losing — unless Ragnarok is already up, which blanks it outright.","Black Cleaver shred plus E true damage make his stacked armor nearly worthless, but his R cooldown keeps it skill-dependent.","You own the duel all game as long as you close before his teamfight R and AoE engage outscale your flat true damage."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"maokai","win":["Olaf","Maokai","Maokai","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"You win first contact: Q-slow into autos while your passive attack speed ramps as you trade, and Maokai has nothing to punish you with before saplings."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"His W root-dash plus Q knockback lock you for free saplings — this is his window, so don't shove into a sapling-stacked wave where he can W you onto the turret."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok blanks his root and knockback for as long as you keep swinging — the peel he leans on stops working and the lane turns back your way."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Bramble/Cleaver online, E's true damage and chained Q-slows shred his tank stats faster than his passive sustain can refund."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his W root-dash, then once it's down chain Q-slows and E-true-damage so his passive can't out-heal the trade","Press Ragnarok before his W lands and keep swinging so the immunity holds","Convert your Levels 1 and 6 windows into prio so his sapling poke never stacks into a wave you can't approach"],"foe":["Land W root-dash and Q knockback to lock you for a free sapling barrage and reset distance","Bait your axes into himself: every spell that strikes him cuts Sap Magic's cooldown and heals him","Drag the lane even and scale his tankiness so your flat true damage stops mattering"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: throw Q to slow him, walk up with autos, and your passive ramps attack speed as you trade — he has no answer before saplings. The catch is Levels 2-3, when his W root-dash plus Q knockback lock you onto a stacked sapling wave for free. He is untargetable through that dash, so never spend E on it; bait the W, and once the root is down the lane is yours again.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a coinflip: Berserker Rage lifesteal and axe-reset slows out-trade his chip, but Sap Magic refunds it — every spell you land on him cuts its cooldown, so burst him rather than grinding. Level 6 is the swing: Ragnarok blanks his root and knockback for as long as you keep swinging, so the peel he relies on stops working. That's your green light to all-in.","late":"First item flips it back your way: Bramble or Black Cleaver plus your E's guaranteed true damage carves through his tank stats faster than Sap Magic can heal, and chained Q-slows mean he never escapes the trade. Outside W he is immobile and easy to isolate, so keep forcing the side-lane all-in. The risk is letting it go even into teamfights, where his front line and a 130s Nature's Grasp outweigh your short-fight kit.","whys":["You own first contact: Q-slow into autos plus passive attack-speed ramp wins level 1, and Maokai has no sapling pressure yet to answer.","His W root-dash plus Q knockback lock you for a free sapling barrage at 2 — he edges this window.","With saplings stacked and W up, his poke-and-peel out-values your single trade before your combo chains — respect his level 3.","Berserker Rage lifesteal trades evenly with Sap Magic and sapling chip — neither side commits cleanly here.","Ragnarok blanks his root and knockback while you swing, but his tankiness holds — an even all-in, not a free kill.","Bramble/Cleaver plus E true damage and chained Q-slows shred his tank stats faster than his passive refunds — your peak.","Against an immobile tank your flat true damage still bites at 2+ items — isolate him in the side lane and dive before teamfights start."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"mel","win":["Skill","Mel","Mel","Skill","Olaf","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Radiant Volley and Solar Snare win levels 2-3 from 950-1000 range before Reckless Swing's 325 can answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes Solar Snare's root useless while you swing, so Undertow slows and Reckless Swing finishes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Black Cleaver/Bramble plus W omnivamp you out-sustain her Q poke and force kill-range all-ins."},{"when":"Late","text":"Rebuttal blanks your burst and reflects projectiles, and Golden Eclipse cashes Overwhelm stacks from any range."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow, then close gap and dump E true damage before she can re-space","Bait Rebuttal out, then commit Reckless Swing after the barrier drops","Hit 6 and use Ragnarok to ignore her W root and E zone for a clean all-in"],"foe":["Poke you down with Q from max range and keep you outside auto range","Hold Rebuttal to blank your all-in and reflect Undertow","Land Solar Snare to peel your dive the moment Ragnarok has expired on you"]},"early":"Mel pokes from outside your range with Q while you only have Q and one of E/W, so levels 1-3 are about eating minimum chip and farming with Q-tip last-hits rather than walking into her line. Do not throw Q as an opener and then walk in dry — she just steps back and Q's you again. Bait her to step up for a CS, land Q to stick the slow, and only commit when you can actually reach her with an auto and E; otherwise back off and let your sustain reset.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you start snowballing short trades: Q-slow to lock her, W on for omnivamp and attack speed, then E true damage that her squishy AP body cannot trade back. The huge swing is 6 — Ragnarok removes her W root and lets you walk through her E execute zone, so all-in the second your ult is up and she has no peel. Just respect her R: if she reflects, your E and autos get bounced back, so make her burn it before you dump damage.","late":"Your kit is flat true damage and short fights, and that fades as Mel stacks AP. Her R reflect turns your E nuke and ramped autos against you, and her E execute zone plus Q poke let her kite and chunk you the moment you over-commit. Your win condition is to have already snowballed lane and dragged the game to dives and objectives by your first-item peak, because once she has 2+ items she reclaims the spacing and you become a lower-impact diver.","whys":["At level 1 she has only Q poke and you have only Q — neither lands a real burst, so first contact is a wash.","Level 2 adds Solar Snare to Radiant Volley, so she roots from 1000 while Reckless Swing needs 325 — she owns the space.","At 3 her Radiant Volley chip stacks Overwhelm before Undertow-into-Reckless Swing closes, so she edges it.","By 4-5 your W omnivamp and ramping passive let you out-sustain her chip, but she can still kite — it's a coin-flip on execution.","Ragnarok ignores Solar Snare's root while you keep swinging, so Undertow slow into Reckless Swing closes it out.","Your first item plus Vicious Strikes fights her first AP item to a draw — Rebuttal still blanks a commit every 33s.","Golden Eclipse detonates Overwhelm from anywhere and Rebuttal blanks your burst, so 2+ items reads even, not yours."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Olaf","Mordekaiser","Olaf","Olaf","Mordekaiser","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into a guaranteed E true-damage nuke chunks Morde before his W shield is worth anything — your peak punish window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Morde's Realm of Death drags you 1v1 and steals your stats — Ragnarok clears disables, not a banish, so it is his biggest swing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble core: your axe-reset perma-slow plus W omnivamp out-sustains his Q-slam-and-W-heal extended fight."},{"when":"Late","text":"At 2+ items full-AP Morde's shield and Q burst out-trade your flat true damage — you must have already snowballed the lead."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick him, then E for guaranteed true damage before his W shield is up","Force short all-ins levels 2-5 where your passive attack speed and W omnivamp win the trade","Bait his E pull, dodge the Q-slam isolation bonus, and punish him on his cooldowns"],"foe":["Land E pull into isolated Q for the empowered slam and W shield value","Banish you with Realm of Death at 6 and steal your stats in a forced 1v1","Survive to 2+ items where his shield-heal sustain out-grinds your flat true damage"]},"early":"Morde is one of the weakest level-1s and so is the trade math for him here — at Level 1 land your Q to slow him, walk up an auto, and your passive attack speed ramps as you take his return. Levels 2-3 are your peak: throw Q to stick him, then E for a guaranteed true-damage chunk he simply can't shield through yet, and pick the axe back up to refund the cooldown so you can perma-slow him out of his own Q-slam range. Dodge his E pull — if he yanks you and lands an isolated Q, that empowered slam plus W shield flips the trade.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay yours: chain axe-reset slows so he can never land an isolated Q, and your W omnivamp heals back his Q-and-W chip in every short all-in. Level 6 is the danger — his R Realm of Death rips you into a 1v1 and steals your stats, and Ragnarok strips CC but can't cleanse the death realm, so don't hold a forward, low-HP fight when his R is up. Bait it or kill him before he reaches it; on his R cooldown you own him again.","late":"You snowball-or-fade, and Morde is a scaler — at 2+ items full-AP Morde's W shield and Q burst start eating your flat true damage, and a stat-stealing R in a teamfight is lethal. Your E nuke and W sustain win the lane phase clean, so convert every level 2-6 lead into plates, kills, and objectives. If this drags past full build with no lead, his isolated-duel kit and R out-trade your short-fight axe damage.","whys":["Morde is a feeble level-1 and your Q-slow-into-auto plus health-scaling passive win first contact outright.","His R is down but at 2 he can land E-pull into an isolated Q-slam plus W shield to flip a sloppy trade — respect the level-2 spike.","Your Q-stick into guaranteed E true damage chunks him before his W shield matters — your hardest punish window.","Axe-reset perma-slows deny his isolated Q while W omnivamp out-sustains his Q-and-W chip in short trades.","Realm of Death drags you 1v1 and steals your stats — Ragnarok clears disables, not banishes, so 6 is his swing.","Your Black Cleaver / bruiser spike with axe slows and W sustain out-grinds his shield-heal — force every all-in here.","On his R cooldown your flat true damage and relentless slows still beat him 1v1 — close it before full build."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"nasus","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Q-slow into autos beats a Nasus who has to walk into Q range to last-hit with his short-range Q stack."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok stops disables, not Wither's slow — bait W first, then Reckless Swing him down inside Fury of the Sands."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble: your oppression peak — perma-Q-slow him off CS and deny his Q stacks before he comes online."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once his Q is stacked and he has Sheen + Spirit Visage, his wither shuts your attack-speed passive off and he out-drains you."}],"wants":{"you":["Chain Q axe-pickups to perma-slow Nasus off his Q last-hits and deny stacks","Bait Wither with a fake step-up, then trade inside its 15s cooldown","Snowball levels 1-6 and dive him before his Q stacks and Spirit Visage land"],"foe":["Wither (W) your passive attack speed to zero so your all-in falls apart","Farm safely with Q under tower and stack toward 300+ before you can dive","Reach 2+ items with Sheen + Spirit Visage and drain you in extended fights"]},"early":"Nasus has to step into 255-range Siphoning Strike to stack, and that is where you live. Throw Undertow to slow him, pick the axe up to reset its 9s, and auto him every time he goes for a minion — your passive ramps attack speed as you take chip, so short trades favor you hard. At level 1 he has no Wither yet; that one level is your freest window, so deny last-hits and keep him off stacks.","mid":"This is still your lane to bully, but Wither is online from level 2 and back every 15s — it cripples your move and attack speed and lands through Ragnarok, so R is not its answer. Bait W out, then commit: Undertow to stick, Vicious Strikes on, Reckless Swing for the true damage. Force the all-in while his Q is still under ~150 stacks; every minute he free-farms is a minute closer to his takeover.","late":"Nasus is the textbook scaler who reclaims this lane — once his Q is stacked and he has Spirit Visage plus Sheen, his wither turns off your attack-speed passive and he out-drains your W omnivamp in any extended fight. Your flat E true damage stops mattering against his health and lifesteal. You had to win this in the first 15 minutes: take his tower, roam, and turn your early lead into objectives before his stacks make him unkillable.","whys":["He must enter Q range to last-hit with his short Q — slow him with Q, reset the axe, and auto while your passive ramps.","Your level-2 Q-plus-auto chip out-trades a Nasus who has no wither and no escape yet.","Even trade window — his Q does real damage on-hit now, so trade only when your axe is up to re-slow him.","You still out-bully him, but Wither is up every 15s and lands through Ragnarok; keep denying Q stacks.","Wither still lands through Ragnarok, and Fury of the Sands tanks your burst — 6 is closer to even than free.","His Q is stacking and Sheen plus Spirit Visage come online — his wither now zeros your passive and he out-drains you.","Fully-stacked Nasus with lifesteal and size shrugs off your flat true damage — close the game before this window."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"nautilus","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E true damage online, you stick Nautilus and chunk a flat health bar his armor can't soften."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's disable immunity holds while you keep swinging — bait Dredge Line, press R, then run him down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble Vest is your oppression peak — perma-slow him and out-sustain his auto-pokes with W omnivamp."},{"when":"Late","text":"His biggest window: in 5v5 he flash-hooks you off your dive and his CC chain lands the moment Ragnarok ends."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to perma-slow Nautilus and chain axe pickups so he can never walk out of your true-damage range","Press Ragnarok before his hook lands, then all-in while Dredge Line is down","Stack early kills and dive him under tower before tank items blunt your E nuke"],"foe":["Land Dredge Line (Q) to pull himself out of your axe slow and reset the trade","Bait Ragnarok out with a hook, then chain his CC back the moment it expires on you","Survive lane, build tank, and turn the game into 5v5 where his CC chain beats your dive"]},"early":"Nautilus trades evenly into you only if you let his autos proc the passive root and his Dredge Line hook lands clean — don't stand in melee letting him stack that. Throw Q to slow him, walk up for an auto, and pull the axe back to reset it so he's permanently slowed and can't reposition. At Level 2-3 your E true damage cuts straight through his tankiness while your passive ramps attack speed as you take his poke — he simply can't match a guaranteed true-damage burst on a flat health bar.","mid":"This is your lane. Keep him perma-slowed with chained Undertow pickups and out-sustain his auto-and-Riptide poke with Vicious Strikes while your short trades snowball. The whole matchup pivots on Ragnarok: press it before Dredge Line lands, not after, because it is disable immunity for as long as you keep attacking — bait the hook, ult, and run him down or dive him under tower. With Bramble/Black Cleaver coming, you're at your most oppressive.","late":"You owned every lane stage, but Nautilus is built for the part of the game where you fade. In 5v5 he flash-hooks you off your backline dive, and his whole CC chain is back up the instant Ragnarok ticks down — your flat true damage matters less against a full tank build while he peels you off carries. Convert your early-to-mid lead into towers and objectives before then; if the game goes long and even, his teamfight CC pulls it back to a coinflip.","whys":["You both have unremarkable level 1s — deny his autos so he can't stack the passive root and set up your Q-slow first contact.","With Q-slow into E true damage you burst a flat health bar his armor can't reduce — he has no answer at 2.","Chained axe pickups keep him perma-slowed while E nukes him; his even trade-pattern can't beat guaranteed true damage.","W omnivamp out-sustains his auto-and-E poke and your short trades snowball — he can't disengage a slowed target.","Ragnarok makes you immune to disables while you keep attacking, so bait Dredge Line and all-in through Riptide.","Black Cleaver / Bramble lets you perma-slow and chunk him every trade — this is your most oppressive lane window.","He out-scales the lane: full-tank Nautilus flash-hooks your dive and his CC chain resets the moment Ragnarok ends."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"neeko","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Olaf","Neeko","Skill","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into a Reckless Swing true-damage hit chunks Neeko for a third of her bar before her root (E) is even leveled."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R: if her clone or a flanking root lands the AOE stun chain, you eat the full combo and Ragnarok is on cooldown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble online — your Q perma-slow plus W-omnivamp lets you walk her down through the root and one-shot her squishy frame."},{"when":"Late","text":"You fall off into her pick potential; reclaim it by diving her under turret with R before she gets a Zhonya's / clone setup."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow, then E true-damage burst before her root (E) cooldown comes back","Hold Ragnarok (R) for her R stun so the all-in lands clean instead of getting chain-CC'd","Snowball levels 2-6 and dive her squishy frame before she buys Zhonya's or sets a clone pick"],"foe":["Land her E root from fog or off a clone (W) to kite you before you can commit","Poke you down with Q tadpole before your W-omnivamp trade window opens","Bait your Ragnarok, then R-stun you after it expires for a free pick"]},"early":"Neeko has no escape and a squishy bar early, and her tadpole Q poke can't out-pace your W-omnivamp once you commit. Throw Q to stick the slow, walk in, and weave Reckless Swing (E) for a guaranteed true-damage chunk she has no way to heal back. The one thing to respect is her root (E) — if it lands she gets a free poke window or a gank set-up, so bait it or step around her cast before you all-in.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay yours: short trades with axe-reset slows and W sustain shred her, and she still folds to one Q-E combo. Level 6 is her window, not yours — her R AOE stun, especially launched from a clone (W) or fog flank, can chain you long enough to delete you, and if your Ragnarok is down you have no answer. Track her clone, hold R for her R, and only dive once her stun or your immunity tells you it's safe.","late":"Late game she becomes a pick threat — a clone-disguised flank into R stun can blow you up before you reach her, and your flat true damage stops one-shotting her once she has Zhonya's or Banshee's. Your job is to never let it get there even: use your level-2-to-first-item dominance to dive her under turret with Ragnarok and snowball the lane shut. If the game drags, force the all-in the instant her R is on cooldown and don't facecheck fog where her clone could be waiting.","whys":["Neeko has no early escape and a squishy bar — your Q-slow into an auto wins first contact before her root matters.","At 2-3 your Q plus Reckless Swing lands guaranteed true damage she can't out-poke or out-heal with tadpole Q.","It's even here: she can level her root (E) and disengage off a clone, but you still threaten the all-in if she steps up.","Levels 4-5 you out-trade her with axe-reset slows and W-omnivamp; her poke can't sustain the short fights you force.","Her R AOE stun, set up from a clone or fog flank, can chain-CC you while your Ragnarok is down — this is her window.","Even at first item: your Black Cleaver/Bramble all-in beats her, but her Zhonya's/clone pick threat keeps it a skill fight.","You reclaim it by diving her squishy frame with Ragnarok before she lands a clone-flank R — close it before her items scale."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"ornn","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Ornn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true-damage burst chunks Ornn before he has any escape — he can't dash or sustain it back."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's immunity holds while you keep swinging, but the pillar is Volcanic Rupture (Q) — deny the terrain and Searing Charge does nothing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble core is your most oppressive lane window — chain-throw Q to perma-slow him and dive before his Sunfire-class HP comes online."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ornn's biggest threat window: 2+ items he is a near-unkillable Brittle-applying frontline whose R+E can airborne you twice for the dive while your true damage stops mattering."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit Level 2-3 first and land Q-slow into E true damage before Ornn can pillar-vault away","Bait Volcanic Rupture’s pillar, then commit where Searing Charge has no terrain to hit","Snowball plates and convert the early lead to dives/objectives before his tank items spike"],"foe":["Use Volcanic Rupture's pillar plus Searing Charge to knock you up and break your all-in apart","Apply Brittle with Bellows Breath to soften you and survive to his forged tank spike","Stall lane even and reach 2+ items where his HP and R double-knockup outscale your flat true damage"]},"early":"Ornn has no sustain and no dash, so Levels 1-3 are yours to take. Land Q to slow him, walk up, and weave E's true-damage nuke into the auto trade — he can't heal it back and can't run from the slow. Watch his E (he dashes a short distance and knocks up if he hits terrain), so don't shove him flush against the wall where his pillar-vault lands cleanly; trade in the open lane where his CC whiffs and your W-omnivamp tops you off.","mid":"Levels 4-5 still favor you — chain axe pickups to perma-slow him and short-trade with Vicious Strikes up while he just farms. At 6 it flattens: Ragnarok's disable immunity carries you in while you keep attacking, but Ornn doesn't need to win the duel — the pillar is Volcanic Rupture (Q), and he vaults off it to safety, eats the trade on tank stats, and calls a gank into all that hard CC. All-in only when Volcanic Rupture is down and you have a path that doesn't end with you airborne under tower.","late":"This is where Ornn flips it. He self-itemizes into a mountain of HP and armor, applies Brittle to amplify the next hit's damage and slow you, and his R sends a charging ram that knocks you up — followed by his own E for a second airborne. Your flat true damage stops scaling and your short fights lose value against his frontline. Your only path is to have already won: take plates, dive on your 6 and first-item spikes, and turn the lead into towers and Grubs/Herald before his tank build comes online.","whys":["No dash, no sustain — your Q-slow-into-auto and passive attack speed win first contact outright.","You hit your Q+E power spike first; one guaranteed true-damage burst chunks an Ornn who can only farm back.","Q-slow lets you stick him for a full E-W trade he has no escape or heal to answer.","Axe-reset slows and W-omnivamp let you win every short trade while he just last-hits with no kill threat.","Ragnarok's disable immunity helps, but he vaults to safety off a pillar and survives on tank stats, so the all-in is not guaranteed — even.","Your Cleaver/Bramble spike is oppressive, yet his self-built HP starts blunting your flat true damage — neither side cleanly owns it.","Full tank Ornn with Brittle plus R+E double-knockup outscales your short-fight kit — your true damage no longer dents him."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"pantheon","win":["Pantheon","Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Pantheon's biggest window: Shield Vault's point-click stun into an empowered Comet Spear out-bursts you before Reckless Swing and Vicious Strikes exist."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Undertow plus Reckless Swing you flip the lane — stick the axe, walk him down, and true damage cuts through Aegis Assault's front-facing block."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's immunity holds while you swing — press it as Shield Vault lands, then all-in or tower-dive him on the spot."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Bramble/Black Cleaver online while Pantheon falls off hard into items — this is your most oppressive window, force every trade before he can scale to relevance."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive his level-1-2 W-stun-into-Q burst, then reach 3 and flip the lane with Q-slow into E true damage","Land Q to stick the slow, then W-omnivamp through his poke so his spear chip never adds up","Press Ragnarok as Shield Vault lands, then all-in while he has no escape"],"foe":["Cheese you at levels 1-2 with W point-click stun plus empowered Q before your E and W come up","Chip you with Comet Spear from 575 range and reset the fight behind Aegis Assault","Use his global R to roam and snowball other lanes since he can't beat you in a straight 1v1 after 3"]},"early":"Pantheon is the one window where you have to be careful — at levels 1-2 Shield Vault's point-click stun into an empowered Comet Spear can chunk you before Reckless Swing and Vicious Strikes are online. Don't walk into a level-1 stun-lock; farm the wave and wait for your spike. The moment you hit 3, the lane flips: land Undertow to stick the slow, walk in, and Reckless Swing for true damage no shield of his reduces — Aegis Assault only blocks what comes at his front.","mid":"This is your lane now. Comet Spear poke can't out-damage Vicious Strikes in any extended trade, and once Undertow sticks he has no dash away — Shield Vault only jumps toward you. At 6 Ragnarok is the dagger: immunity to his stun for as long as you keep attacking, so press it as he vaults in and run him down or dive him under tower. With Bramble or Black Cleaver online you are at your most oppressive while he's already falling off.","late":"You stay ahead here in a way you don't against true scalers — Pantheon falls off into items even harder than you do, so your flat true damage still matters against him. The only thing that saves him is his global R roaming to other lanes, so don't let him farm-and-roam back into the game. Convert your lane lead into towers, the rift herald, and dives before he becomes a teamfight ult-flank instead of a laner you can just kill.","whys":["Pantheon owns level 1: his W point-click stun plus empowered Q out-bursts you before your E true damage or W sustain exist.","It evens out at 2 — you have a slow and a trade tool, but Comet Spear pokes from 575 and Shield Vault stuns every 13s.","With Undertow into Reckless Swing you flip it — true damage ignores everything he builds, and Shield Vault dashes at you, never away from you.","Your W-omnivamp out-sustains his spear poke and your axe-reset slows let you walk him down all-in after all-in.","Ragnarok makes you immune to Shield Vault's stun while you keep swinging — press it on his dash and run him down.","Your Bramble/Black Cleaver spike lands while Pantheon already falls off into items — force every trade now.","You keep beating him late because he scales worse than you do — only his global R roam saves him, so close the map before that matters."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"poppy","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Undertow into Reckless Swing chunks Poppy before Hammer Shock's zone or a wall stun can answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok answers Heroic Charge's stun while you keep attacking, and Steadfast Presence has no dash of yours to stop."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble peak — your true damage and omnivamp shred her tank build and out-sustain her passive shield."},{"when":"Late","text":"Poppy's biggest window: full-build she peels your dive with E-wall stun + R knockback and protects her carries while your flat true damage falls off."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow to stick her, then E her for guaranteed true damage she can't shield through","Pop W-omnivamp in extended trades so her passive-shield poke can't out-sustain you","Press Ragnarok as Heroic Charge lands, then all-in before her tank items arrive"],"foe":["Pin you to a wall with Heroic Charge for the stun while your R is down","Stack tank items and collect her Iron Ambassador buckler shield to outscale you","Save E-wall and R knockback to peel your dive off her carries in teamfights"]},"early":"Poppy trades evenly into a lot of champs because Steadfast Presence eats dashes, but you have no dashes for it to eat, so half her kit is dead weight here. At Level 2-3 land Undertow to slow her, walk in, and Reckless Swing for the burst, then back off before Heroic Charge can angle you into a wall for the stun. Fight in open lane away from walls, and step off Hammer Shock's zone before it explodes.","mid":"Through Levels 4-5 keep chaining axe resets to perma-slow her and stack short trades; your passive ramps attack speed as you take her poke, and Vicious Strikes heals it back faster than she can re-collect her buckler. At 6 Ragnarok answers Heroic Charge: press it as she dashes in and the stun does nothing while you keep swinging. This is your kill window before she finishes tank items.","late":"Once Poppy is full-build the lane inverts on the map. Her E-wall stun and R knockback exist to peel exactly your kind of dive, so in teamfights she can wall you off her carry and ult you out the moment your Ragnarok ends. Your flat true damage stops scaling while her tank stats climb, so don't try to solo-dive through her late — convert the early lead into towers, plates and objectives before the game reaches her item spikes.","whys":["You win first contact with Q-slow-into-auto and your passive attack speed; her W can't stop a dash you don't have.","Your Level 2 Q+E lands a guaranteed true-damage chunk Poppy's passive shield can't fully absorb.","With Q, W and E online you out-trade her short pokes and her E pin can't save her in open lane.","Axe-reset slows plus W-omnivamp snowball every short trade; she has no sustain to match.","Ragnarok’s immunity holds while you swing, and her Q is a slow zone, not a knockup — your best window.","Your Black Cleaver / Bramble spike with true damage out-paces her first tank item.","Full-build Poppy peels your dive with E-wall and R and outscales your flat true damage — play for objectives, not solo dives."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"quinn","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Quinn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Open with a Q axe to land the slow, then walk up and auto — your passive attack speed already beats her cooldown-gated poke when she can't kite a slowed melee."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"The blind is Blinding Assault (Q), not Vault — eat it, ult for the immunity, re-throw Undertow to stick her, and Reckless Swing while Vault is on its 12s."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Black Cleaver and W's omnivamp up your all-in heals through her Harrier poke — chain Q axe pickups to perma-slow and she has no second escape."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past two items she kites with Harrier move speed and roams; if you haven't ended she pokes you out before you reach her and out-rotates you on the map."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q axe slows and pick the axe back up to chain-slow her so Harrier move speed can't open a gap","Press Ragnarok the moment she spends Vault, then Reckless Swing her for true damage","Win lanes 1-6 and snowball before her ranged poke and roams take over the map"],"foe":["Hold Vault to leap out of your slow and reset the fight every time you commit","Kite with Harrier passive move speed and chip you with poke from outside Q range","Roam and scale into a poke/pick threat once you fall off past two items"]},"early":"Quinn wants to poke you from range with Harrier procs and never let you walk up, but her cooldowns are the opening — lead with Undertow to slow her, then close and auto while your passive attack speed ramps. Don't blow Reckless Swing into thin air the second you reach her; Vault leaps her back out and resets the trade. Bait Vault, eat Blinding Assault on your autos, then pick the axe up to re-stick her and follow up. You out-damage her short trades through level 3 as long as the slow lands.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you snowball every short trade — axe pickups reset Undertow off its flat 9s so she is never unslowed, and Vicious Strikes heals the Harrier poke right back. Level 6 is the kill window: press Ragnarok for the immunity, glue her with Undertow, and Reckless Swing for true damage she cannot vault away from. Her only out is Flash or a missed axe — punish her the instant Vault is on its 12s.","late":"This is her game if you let it get here. Past two items Quinn kites with Harrier move speed, vaults away from every Q, and chips you down before you ever land an axe — and she roams to take over the map while you're stuck split. Your flat true damage and short-fight kit stop being enough. Convert your early lead into towers, dives, and objectives before ~20 minutes; if the game goes long, she pokes you out and out-rotates you.","whys":["Your Q slow into autos wins first contact — her Harrier poke can't kite a melee she can't outrun, and your passive ramps as you trade.","At 2 with Q plus E you land a guaranteed true-damage burst her cooldown-gated poke can't match before her vault is reliably up.","Chain Q axe pickups to perma-slow her and E through the gap — she has no second escape once the vault is down.","Your axe-reset slows plus W omnivamp out-sustain her Harrier chip in every short trade through 4-5.","Ragnarok's immunity holds while you swing — ult, re-throw Undertow to stick her, and Reckless Swing for the kill.","Black Cleaver plus W omnivamp is your most oppressive point — your all-in heals through her poke and the slow never lets her kite.","Past two items she kites with Harrier move speed, vaults your Q, and pokes you out before you commit, then out-roams you on the map."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"renekton","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once you have Q plus E you land a guaranteed true-damage burst Renekton's auto-and-W combo can't match in a short trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok's immunity holds while you swing, so Ruthless Predator's 1.5s empowered stun does nothing at all."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Black Cleaver / Bramble core and W-omnivamp you out-sustain his fury combos at your most oppressive lane point."},{"when":"Late","text":"Renekton's biggest danger is a fed early lead snowballed before 6 — if even, his fury combos fade and you both lose solo-carry weight."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick Q-slow on him and trade short bursts with E true damage his armor can't reduce","Reach 6 and press Ragnarok as Ruthless Predator lands, then commit hard","Use W-omnivamp to heal back his fury-combo poke and win every extended trade"],"foe":["Land empowered Ruthless Predator to strip your shield and stun you for a full 1.5s","Bully levels 1-3 with point-and-click damage while his fury is up and your axe is on cooldown","Get an early snowball lead because his only window is before items and your 6"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are the one stretch Renekton can fight you: his W is a point-click stun and his fury-empowered Q+E combo bursts hard before you scale. Don't sit in his auto range with your axe (Q) on cooldown — throw Q to land the slow, then pick the axe up to refund the cooldown and chain another slow so he can't reset distance. Once you hit Level 2-3 with Q plus E you have a guaranteed true-damage nuke his armor does nothing against, and your passive ramps your attack speed as you take his combo.","mid":"This is where you take over. Through levels 4-5 your axe-reset slows perma-stick him and Vicious Strikes heals back every fury combo he lands, so short trades go your way. At 6 Ragnarok answers his whole kit: press it as Ruthless Predator lands and the stun does nothing while you keep attacking, then Reckless Swing his health bar down. Bait W out — once it is down at 16s he has no point-click peel at all.","late":"If you played the early even, you win — Renekton falls off hard into items and has no sustained threat once you survive his fury windows, while your bruiser core and W-omnivamp keep beating him in the duel. The real risk is the reverse: if he got an early snowball before your 6, his fury combos can still chunk you. Convert your lane lead into dives and objectives, because at 2+ items both of you lose solo-carry weight and the game shifts to teamfights where your Ragnarok dive still matters more than his short-trade burst.","whys":["Both of you are strong level-1 bullies — his point-click W-and-auto poke trades even with your Q-slow-into-auto before anyone has a burst.","You hit your Q+E guaranteed true-damage combo first and his armor doesn't reduce it, beating his fury auto trade.","Axe-reset slows let you stick him while E true damage cuts through his early armor — his combo can't out-burst yours.","W-omnivamp heals back his fury poke and your reset slows keep him in short trades you win clearly.","Ragnarok makes you immune to Ruthless Predator's stun while you keep swinging, so his whole all-in setup does nothing.","Your Black Cleaver / bruiser spike with W sustain out-trades his fury combos at your most oppressive lane point.","He falls off hard into items but so do you — at 2+ items neither solo-carries, so the lane reads even unless someone snowballed."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"riven","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Riven"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into auto then E true damage is your cleanest burst before she has her full three-dash Q chain and shield up."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes Ki Burst's stun useless while you keep attacking — soak the combo, then Reckless Swing once her dashes are spent."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble keeps your lane pressure oppressive, but her Q-reset combo and Conqueror stacking start matching your trade damage."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once she has two items her three-dash mobility, E shield and burst window let her sidestep your Q and reset trades you can't catch."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to slow her and remove a dash window, then walk in for an E true-damage hit before she can Q-dash away","Bait her E shield and W stun out early, then all-in while they are on cooldown with W omnivamp running","Press Ragnarok as Ki Burst lands so her stun does nothing at all while you keep swinging"],"foe":["Sidestep your Q with her three Q dashes so the slow never sticks and your axe-reset pressure dies","Catch you mid-animation with Ki Burst's stun while Ragnarok is down, then burst inside her combo window","Stall lane to two items where her mobility and Conqueror-stacked resets out-trade your flat true damage"]},"early":"Level 1-2 are yours: lead with Q to slow her, pick the axe back up to refund the cooldown, and chain another Q-auto before she can space you. The instant you hit 2-3 you have Q plus E, and her early Q-dash chain plus E shield aren't enough sustain to eat a guaranteed E true-damage hit on top of your slowed autos. Don't waste E chasing a full-stack Riven who can three-dash out — land the Q first so the slow takes a dash window away, then E.","mid":"This is the even stretch — she gets her Conqueror stacking and her full Broken Wings combo, so respect that she can burst you inside her window if she catches you mid-axe-throw with Ki Burst. Your answer is discipline: keep her perma-slowed with axe resets so she can't space, and pop Vicious Strikes for the attack speed and shield in any extended trade. At 6, Ragnarok is the equalizer — press it as Ki Burst lands, soak the combo, and Reckless Swing her out once her dashes are spent.","late":"From two items she pulls ahead. Her three-dash mobility lets her sidestep your Q so the slow never lands, and her E shield plus burst window let her trade-reset faster than your flat true damage can punish. Your Ragnarok is now a single fight-immunity button on a long cooldown, not a lane crutch. You have to have converted the early-game lead into plates, kills, or Herald before this point — if it's an even farm game at 25 minutes, she has the better scaling 1v1 and the better teamfight reset.","whys":["Your Q-slow into auto plus passive attack speed wins first contact before she has any dashes charged.","At 2 you have Q plus E for a guaranteed true-damage burst her E shield can't fully eat yet.","She gets her full three-dash Q and shield online, so she can dodge your Q and reset — it's a spacing duel now.","W omnivamp keeps your trades even, but her Conqueror stacking and combo damage match you when she lands it.","Ragnarok's immunity to Ki Burst holds while you keep swinging, but a good Riven just dashes away — it nets even.","Black Cleaver / Bramble keeps you oppressive, yet her Q-reset burst trades back evenly into your bruiser core.","Her two-item mobility sidesteps your Q and her shield resets trades your flat true damage can no longer punish."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"rumble","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Lead Q on the wave, walk up on the axe and auto — your passive attack speed already out-trades a pre-heat Rumble before Flamespitter ramps."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok does not clear Electro Harpoon's slow, but Reckless Swing's true damage ignores his MR — commit through the burn."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver + W-omnivamp: you all-in through Flamespitter, healing the burn while your E ignores his magic resist entirely."},{"when":"Late","text":"His danger window — once he has Liandry's/Rylai's he pokes you down with E-into-Flamespitter and zones you off objectives with Equalizer before you reach him."}],"wants":{"you":["Pick the axe up to refund Undertow and chain the slow so Scrap Shield's speed never saves him","Ignore Electro Harpoon, it holds two charges — commit on his cold heat gauge instead","Press Ragnarok when he commits Equalizer, then Reckless Swing him down inside it"],"foe":["Pre-heat Flamespitter to the overheat threshold before you engage so his DPS spikes mid-trade","Land E harpoon to slow your walk-up and proc the bonus on his next Flamespitter tick","Drop Equalizer between you and him to zone your engage and chunk you as you cross it"]},"early":"Rumble has no point-and-click answer to a committed Olaf early — lead with Q to slow him, walk up on the axe to refund the cooldown, and auto while your passive ramps your attack speed. He'll want to pre-heat Flamespitter before he fights, so punish him when his heat gauge is cold and his W shield isn't up. Don't sit in the Flamespitter cone trading autos for free; step in with Q-slow, land your hits, and step out — your sustain wins the math every time.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep snowballing short trades: Undertow into Reckless Swing cuts straight through his magic resist, and Vicious Strikes heals the Flamespitter chip back. At 6 Ragnarok is the lane-ender — but it clears disables, not the Electro Harpoon slow, so the plan is to eat the burn and keep swinging rather than expect to be freed. Commit when he spends Equalizer and run him down before Scrap Shield's speed burst reaches tower.","late":"This is where Rumble flips it. Once he has Liandry's and Rylai's, his E-into-Flamespitter poke chunks you before you can force a melee all-in, and Equalizer zones you off every objective and teamfight chokepoint. Your flat true damage and short-fight kit lose value while his AOE scales. Convert your early-to-mid lead into towers, plates, and dives now — take the lane before ~20 minutes so his scaling never gets to decide the game.","whys":["Rumble can't trade a cold Flamespitter into your Q-slow walk-up — your passive attack speed wins first contact.","With Q plus an auto chain you out-DPS a pre-heat Rumble before his W shield and overheat come online.","Q-slow into E's guaranteed true damage cuts through his magic resist while your axe-reset keeps him stuck.","You out-sustain his Flamespitter chip with W-omnivamp, snowballing short trades he can't disengage from.","Ragnarok blanks his disables, not the harpoon slow — press it, eat the burn, and Reckless Swing him down.","Black Cleaver plus W-omnivamp lets you all-in through Flamespitter; your E ignores his MR and your heal eats the burn.","He out-scales: Liandry's/Rylai's E-into-Flamespitter pokes you out and Equalizer zones objectives before you commit."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"ryze","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Olaf","Ryze"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into an E true-damage nuke chunks Ryze before his Q/E root combo can stack a kill — your guaranteed burst beats his early."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes you immune to Rune Prison — his only hard CC — so from 6 you walk through his lockdown and all-in him uncontested."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble plus W-omnivamp is your oppression peak — perma-slow him with axe resets and out-sustain his poke."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Ryze hits 2+ items his Overload resets out-DPS you — Spell Flux into Rune Prison roots you at 615 range and he bursts you from there."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow then E true damage to force short all-ins his root combo can't survive","Hit 6 and use Ragnarok to ignore his Q/E/W roots and dive him on cooldown","End the lane on your first-item spike before his Q resets and shield come online"],"foe":["Land Spell Flux then Rune Prison to root you out of melee range and poke you","Use his Flux-primed root to break your all-in and stall to 2+ items","Scale his Q reset chain and mana pool into a raid-boss that kites and bursts you"]},"early":"Ryze can't kill you early — his Overload poke and E-into-W root combo cost a lot of mana and don't out-damage your sustain. At level 1 your Q-slow into an auto wins first contact, and by 2-3 you have Q plus E to land a guaranteed true-damage nuke he can't match. Dodge Spell Flux — with no Flux on you, Rune Prison only slows; if he burns E on minions, walk up, throw Q, then E him. Don't let his slows kite you off the wave.","mid":"This is your takeover window. Chase him with axe resets to perma-slow, W on for omnivamp to heal his poke back, and E for true damage that ignores his magic resist. At 6 Ragnarok is the trump card: pop it and Rune Prison — his one piece of lockdown, 11s at rank 1 — cannot stop you, so all-in or tower-dive him. Force every fight here; his only out is flashing the root and praying for jungle.","late":"From two items on, Ryze becomes the problem. His Overload resets and Flux chain start to out-DPS your flat true damage, Spell Flux into Rune Prison roots you at 615 to break your gap-close, and he kites you while Realm Warp repositions his team. Your job is to have already won — convert your early-to-mid lead into towers, plates and dives before ~20-25 min. If it goes long, group with your team and look to dive him before he gets to free-cast; never duel a full-build Ryze alone.","whys":["Your Q-slow-into-auto wins first contact and Ryze's lone Q poke can't trade back at level 1.","With Q plus E you land a guaranteed true-damage burst that his single-target poke can't answer yet.","Your axe slow sticks him for the E nuke before Spell Flux into Rune Prison can root you.","You out-trade and W-omnivamp back his poke while his mana drains from spamming Q to farm safely.","Ragnarok makes you immune to Rune Prison, his only lockdown, so you dive straight through his defense.","Black Cleaver plus W sustain is your oppression peak — perma-slow and out-heal him before his resets scale.","He out-scales hard: Overload resets and Flux-primed Rune Prison let him kite and burst you once he has two items."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"sejuani","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E's guaranteed true damage you out-burst her, and Arctic Assault is down 18s at rank 1 the moment she spends it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes you immune to disables while you keep attacking — Permafrost, Glacial Prison and her knock-up all stop mattering."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver plus your E true damage rips through the armour Fury of the North stacks on top of her tank items."},{"when":"Late","text":"Glacial Prison lands from 1300 range and swings whole teamfights while your flat true damage falls off — her one window."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to perma-slow her so she can never walk out of your E true-damage range","Hit Level 6 and Ragnarok through Permafrost and Glacial Prison to all-in","Bait her E-stun, then commit your W-sustain trade while it is on cooldown"],"foe":["Hold her E-stun for jungle ganks rather than burning it in a losing 1v1","Stack Frost with Winter's Wrath and land Permafrost in drawn-out fights","Survive lane and save Glacial Prison for the 5v5 teamfights where she scales"]},"early":"Sejuani has exactly one gap-closer, Arctic Assault, and at 18s on rank 1 she cannot reach you again for a long time once she spends it — bait it, then trade. Note Fury of the North makes her slow-immune out of combat, so your first axe only bites after she has already taken damage. Respect Permafrost: it stuns only at full Frost stacks, so bait the stacks out, then commit your Tough It Out trade.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are your takeover. Your Q-reset slows keep her glued in place while E nukes through her tankiness, and your passive ramps attack speed as Winter's Wrath chips you. At 6 Ragnarok is the whole matchup: while you keep attacking you are immune to disables, so Permafrost and Glacial Prison cannot stop the all-in or the tower dive. Force the kill or burn her Flash here, because every plate you take is a lead she cannot scale back into lane.","late":"Late game is the one place she gets even. Glacial Prison stuns from 1300 range on a 90s rank-3 cooldown while your flat E true damage and short-trade kit lose value once carries are full-build. Do not let the game drift to 35-minute teamfights where she peels for someone, instead convert your lane lead into towers, Heralds and dives before 2+ items so the map is already won when her engage comes online.","whys":["Q-slow into an auto wins first contact, and Arctic Assault is down 18s at rank 1 if she opens with it.","Q plus E lands a guaranteed true-damage burst she cannot match, and Permafrost only fires on full Frost stacks she cannot build yet.","Your axe-reset slow perma-sticks her while E shreds through armor she built to be tanky.","You out-trade Winter's Wrath with Tough It Out's shield and a passive that hits faster the lower you drop.","Ragnarok makes you immune to Permafrost, Glacial Prison and her knock-up while you keep attacking her.","Black Cleaver and E true damage strip her armor faster than her W and passive can punish you back.","Glacial Prison and tank scaling reclaim teamfights while your flat true damage falls off, so close it before this window."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"sett","win":["Olaf","Skill","Sett","Sett","Olaf","Sett","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Lead with Undertow (Q) — the slow sticks Sett and your auto cracks him before his passive double-punch can stack on you."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Sett has W stored and his passive rhythm going he wins the grit war — his true-damage smash punishes your E self-damage trades."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes you immune to Facebreaker and The Show Stopper while you keep swinging — his all-in becomes your free dive."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Sett's Bami/bruiser core plus stored W out-sustains your Black Cleaver trades — his most oppressive lane point, not yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Open with Q-slow into auto and reset the axe to perma-slow Sett before his passive stacks","Save Ragnarok for Facebreaker into Haymaker and keep swinging through it","Use E true damage to dive him under tower once his R is on cooldown"],"foe":["Catch you between him and a minion so Facebreaker stuns instead of only slowing","Build W charge in extended trades so his true-damage smash out-chunks your E","Land The Show Stopper to flip your all-in and combo you down"]},"early":"Open with Undertow (Q) — the slow lets you walk an auto onto Sett before Pit Grit's rhythm gets going, and picking the axe back up resets it. Don't sit in extended trades at level 1-2: his alternating punches and Grit shield ramp the longer you swing, and every point of Reckless Swing self-damage is Grit he cashes back. Facebreaker only stuns when enemies are on both sides of him — stand clear of the minion line and it is only a slow.","mid":"This is Sett's window, not yours — by levels 3-5 he has Haymaker stored, Pit Grit is punching every other auto, and his true-damage smash out-chunks your Reckless Swing trades since E costs you health he cashes as Grit. Respect Facebreaker (16s at rank 1); if he catches you between himself and a minion it stuns instead of slowing and the full Haymaker follows. Hold your ground only when his Grit bar is empty and Facebreaker is down. At 6 the lane flips for one moment: Ragnarok makes you immune to disables while you keep swinging, so bait his all-in and ult through it with your passive attack speed ramping.","late":"Past first item Sett's stored Haymaker plus his bruiser sustain out-grinds your short-trade kit, and your flat E true damage stops scaling while The Show Stopper stays teamfight-relevant. You don't out-scale him, so your job is to cash your level 6 R window into kills, plates, or a herald before two items — once he's full bruiser the straight 1v1 is a coinflip you'd rather not take. In skirmishes, Ragnarok still lets you keep swinging through his ultimate onto a backliner.","whys":["Your Q-slow into auto wins first contact before Sett's passive double-punch and grit can stack against you.","It's a wash by level 2 — his stored W and passive ramp answer your Q poke, so neither of you cleanly owns the trade.","With W charged and E grab online Sett's true-damage smash out-chunks your E self-damage trades.","His passive rhythm plus W sustain grind down your short trades through levels 4-5 while your E costs you health.","Ragnarok makes you immune to Facebreaker and The Show Stopper while you keep swinging, so you all-in through his CC.","Sett's first-item bruiser core and stored W out-sustain your Black Cleaver poke — his most oppressive point.","Your E true damage stops scaling while Haymaker's shield grows off your damage, so two-item duels are a coinflip."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"shen","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Shen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks Shen before his W shield is worth slotting — your cleanest early all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes you immune to Shadow Dash's taunt while you keep swinging — his only CC stops working."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver plus axe resets keep Shen perma-slowed, so Shadow Dash is his only way out of the trade."},{"when":"Late","text":"Stand United (160s at rank 3) and his stacked resists outvalue your flat true damage once he has 2+ items."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow and pick the axe back up to perma-slow Shen into repeated E true-damage trades","Bait Shadow Dash or hold Ragnarok to swing through the taunt, then all-in","Snowball levels 1-6 and dive him before his resists and Stand United matter"],"foe":["Block your autos inside Spirit's Refuge to deny your passive attack-speed ramp","Land Shadow Dash to lock your all-in and trade evenly while he scales","Stall the lane even and use Stand United to make plays elsewhere, then outscale in teamfights"]},"early":"Shen has no early kill threat — Spirit's Refuge only blocks basic attacks inside his spirit blade's zone, and Twilight Assault is weak pre-items. Land Undertow to slow (it is an ability, so the refuge does not stop it), walk up and E for the guaranteed true-damage chunk. The one thing to respect is Shadow Dash, 600 range on 18s at rank 1: bait the taunt before you commit, and don't burn Ragnarok early.","mid":"Levels 4-6 stay yours. Keep picking the axe back up to perma-slow him, force short trades where Tough It Out's shield covers his chip, and his only answer is Shadow Dash — 18s at rank 1, so the moment he spends it the lane is yours. At 6, Ragnarok makes you immune to the taunt while you keep swinging, so dive him. Shove and crash to deny his roam value before his scaling kicks in.","late":"This flips. Shen's whole point is the late game: stacked resists and Ki Barrier tank your DPS, Stand United lets him impact a map you can't reach on a 160s rank-3 cooldown, and your flat E true damage stops scaling. Convert your early-to-mid lead into towers and dives BEFORE 2 items — if the game goes even into the mid-game, Shen's utility and global presence quietly out-values your snowball-or-fade kit.","whys":["Shen can't punish your level-1 Q-slow-into-auto, and Spirit's Refuge blocks autos he has no trade behind.","Your Q plus E true-damage burst chunks him harder than his Q empower can answer.","Axe resets stick him for a second Reckless Swing before Spirit's Refuge is back up.","Tough It Out out-sustains his chip and his only CC, Shadow Dash, is down 18s at rank 1.","Ragnarok blocks his taunt while you swing, but Ki Barrier lets Shen survive the dive — even.","Your Black Cleaver spike is oppressive, yet his bulk and global R give him outs — neither side clearly wins.","Ki Barrier, resist stacking and Stand United outscale your flat true damage once he hits 2+ items."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"singed","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Skill","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Land Q to slow him, walk up and chunk with autos plus E true damage before Fling (10s) and Poison Trail ramp."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok lets you keep swinging through his CC, but Fling is a displacement it will not stop — respect it even with R up."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your Bramble Vest / Black Cleaver core is your last clean window to all-in before his Rylai's and Liandry's let him kite forever."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once he has Rylai's and Liandry's, Noxious Slipstream plus Mega Adhesive let him fling you into a root and run you down through your true damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow, then walk up and trade autos plus E true damage in a short window","Hold Ragnarok for the poison chase, not for Fling — it will not stop it","Cut his proxy farm by holding wave and forcing him to fight, then snowball before he scales"],"foe":["Proxy the wave behind your tower to dodge your Q and deny you a clean all-in","Fling you back into Poison Trail and Mega Adhesive so you are rooted in the goo he laid","Stack Rylai's plus Liandry's and scale into an uncatchable, unkillable run-you-down monster"]},"early":"Singed is one of the few champs who can just walk away from your Q-slow, because Noxious Slipstream gives him a speed burst every time he passes you, so do not throw axes into open ground he can sidestep. Aim Q to land directly on him when he steps up to last-hit, then walk in and stack autos plus an E true-damage tick while your passive attack speed ramps. He has no early damage besides Poison Trail, so a clean Q-into-E trade chunks him hard before he can Fling you. Watch for him proxying behind your tower instead of fighting.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you still out-trade him, but Fling becomes the whole fight: at 125 range on 10s it throws you behind him, and if he has dropped Mega Adhesive where you land you are rooted in the poison, so trade only when Fling is down. At 6, Ragnarok lets you keep swinging through his CC — but Fling is a displacement it does not stop, and Insanity Potion makes Poison Trail apply Grievous Wounds, which cuts the lifesteal Berserker Rage gives you. This lane tilts toward who controls the wave: if he proxies, deny it and freeze to force him to walk into your Q.","late":"This is where Singed takes over. Once he has Rylai's, Liandry's and Demonic Embrace, Fling plus the permanent Mega Adhesive slow means your flat E true damage and short trades stop mattering, and Noxious Slipstream lets him run you down or simply walk away whenever he wants. You cannot catch a Singed who does not want to be caught, and Insanity Potion's Grievous Wounds cuts your lifesteal in every extended fight. Your only path is to have already converted the early lead into towers, plates and objectives before he comes online, then group rather than try to 1v1 him.","whys":["Your Q-slow into auto plus passive attack speed wins first contact before Poison Trail or Fling can punish you.","With Q plus E you land a guaranteed true-damage burst his poison tick cannot trade back.","Q-reset slows let you chain a short all-in and W-omnivamp heals the poison chip he leaves on you.","Fling into Poison Trail flips short trades, and Mega Adhesive roots you where he drops you — a coin-flip window.","Ragnarok blocks disables, but Fling is a displacement it ignores and his ult anti-heals your lifesteal.","Your Bramble / Black Cleaver spike pressures him, but his first Rylai's lets him kite the all-in, so it is even.","Full build he flings you into goo, roots you there and runs you down through your flat true damage."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"sion","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks Sion before Soul Furnace is leveled enough to absorb it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes you immune to the stun on a charged Decimating Smash while you keep swinging — his peel stops working."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble core: your axe-reset slows perma-stick him and your peak lane pressure forces dives."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Sion's biggest window is here, when his W shield and zombie passive make him an unkillable HP sponge your flat true damage can't shred fast enough."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow to stick him, then weave E true damage that ignores his stacked armor","Reach level 6 and swing through his charged Decimating Smash stun with R","Snowball lanes/towers before 2 items so his tank scaling never gets online"],"foe":["Land a fully charged Q knockup to peel your all-in and trade safely","Soak your trades behind Soul Furnace and poke with Roar of the Slayer","Stall lane to 2+ items where his HP pool and Glory in Death outlast your true damage"]},"early":"Sion is exactly the immobile melee you farm: no dash to dodge your Q, so your axe-slow sticks every time and your passive ramps attack speed as you take his poke. Respect two things — a charged Decimating Smash stuns and knocks up, so trade on its 10s cooldown or bait it and step in, and Roar of the Slayer fired through a minion knocks that minion into you and shreds your armour. At 2-3, Q-slow into E bursts him before Soul Furnace is big enough to eat it.","mid":"This is your takeover window. Keep chaining Q pickups to perma-slow him so he can't walk to last-hits, and E him whenever it's up — that true damage cuts straight through the armor he's stacking. At 6, Ragnarok is the whole matchup: while you keep swinging you are immune to the stun on his charged Decimating Smash, the only tool he has to stop your dive, so all-in on its cooldown and he cannot peel.","late":"Sion is the rare tank who reclaims this lane late, not early — once he has two items Soul Furnace, raw HP and Glory in Death turn him into a sponge your flat E true damage can't burn through fast enough. Killing him is not the end either: the revive brings him back with rapid attacks that heal him and scale off your max health. Don't let it get there: convert your early-to-mid kill pressure into plates, towers and dives before his scaling matters, and if it goes long use Ragnarok to dive past him onto his carries.","whys":["No dash means your Q-slow sticks his first contact and your passive attack speed wins the level-1 auto trade.","Your Q-into-auto chunk out-trades Roar of the Slayer's armour-shred poke before Soul Furnace scales.","Q-slow plus E true damage bursts him while his W shield is still too small to absorb it.","Axe resets perma-stick him and Tough It Out's shield covers his poke through 4-5.","Ragnarok makes you immune to the stun on his charged Decimating Smash while you keep swinging.","Your bruiser-core lane pressure forces dives his immobile kit can't answer at first item.","From two items Soul Furnace, his HP pool and Glory in Death sponge your flat true damage — it levels out."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"swain","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Swain"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks Swain before Nevermove is even up — your first guaranteed kill window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes you immune to Nevermove's root while you keep swinging, so his one peel tool stops working."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver plus Bramble shred and anti-heal blunt his Soul Fragment healing in every extended trade."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Swain hits 2+ items Demonic Ascension drains everything around him faster than your flat true damage kills — his window."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow, then all-in before Nevermove and Demonic Ascension","Hold Ragnarok for his E-root so you cleanse it and dive him during W-bomb peel","End the lane on your level 2-6 spikes before his Soul Fragment stacks pile up"],"foe":["Root you on Nevermove's return pass and pull you in, then poke with Death's Hand","Stack Soul Fragments off Vision of Empire and drain-heal through extended fights","Survive to 2+ items where Demonic Ascension out-sustains your short fights"]},"early":"Swain has no answer to your level 1-3 pressure — a slow, immobile drain-mage with no dash. Open with Q to land the slow, walk in, and weave E's true damage; Death's Hand and Vision of Empire cannot match a guaranteed Reckless Swing chunk. The one thing to respect is Nevermove: the outgoing wave does nothing, the RETURN pass is what roots you, so watch it come back and sidestep that, not the throw.","mid":"This is your takeover. Through 4-5 your axe resets and Tough It Out's shield let you sit on him in every short trade, and his pre-6 kit cannot peel you off. At 6 Ragnarok is the lane-winner — while you keep swinging you are immune to Nevermove's root, and its passive armour and MR blunt his magic damage, so you ult into his peel and run him down or tower-dive. Don't ult into nothing; save it for when he commits Nevermove.","late":"You have to close this before it goes long. Once Swain reaches 2+ items Demonic Ascension is a sustained drain off every nearby champion, minion and monster, healing him faster than you can trade, and Nevermove roots your carries from 850 and pulls them in while you tunnel one target. Your flat E true damage and short-fight kit lose value here — so convert every early lead into towers, dives and objectives and never let this become a 30-minute scaling fight.","whys":["Swain has no dash and only Death's Hand at level 1 — your Q-slow-into-auto wins first contact outright.","Your Q-into-E true-damage burst lands before Nevermove is reliable, and he cannot escape the slow.","With Q, W and E you chain a slow-locked all-in that Death's Hand and Vision of Empire cannot answer.","Axe resets and Tough It Out's shield out-trade his poke every short fight while he is still peel-less.","Ragnarok makes you immune to Nevermove's root while you swing, so his only peel fails and you dive.","Bramble plus Black Cleaver out-damage Death's Hand and his drain at your most oppressive point.","Demonic Ascension drains from everything nearby and out-sustains your flat true damage from two items."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"sylas","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Sylas"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks Sylas before Kingslayer can heal it back - your best early window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Sylas R steals your Ragnarok - he gets a free CC-immune dive ult, so this is HIS spike, not yours."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble: your sustained all-in still out-trades a one-rotation Sylas if you stick the Q-slow."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-AP Sylas heals off Kingslayer and dashes away on Abscond once your true damage stops scaling."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to perma-slow Sylas so he cannot walk out of Reckless Swing range","All-in at 2-3 with E true damage before Kingslayer heals it back","Save your kill pressure for when Abscond is on its 13s cooldown"],"foe":["Steal your Ragnarok with his R to get a free CC-immune all-in or escape","Heal off Kingslayer and chip you with Chain Lash before you commit","Scale to 2+ AP items where his sustain and burst out-trade your flat true damage"]},"early":"Sylas is also melee, so you actually get to fight - this isn't a kiter lane. Land your Q to slow him and walk him down; at 2-3 your E true damage burst beats anything Kingslayer heals back. He carries two dashes - Kingslayer's lunge and Abscond, which recasts into a chain pull - so bait one out before you commit, because Abscond is 13s at rank 1. Chain Lash's cross explodes on a delay, so step off the intersection.","mid":"You're still favored through 4-5 - axe resets plus Tough It Out's shield out-grind his rotations. But level 6 flips: Hijack steals YOUR Ragnarok on an 80s cooldown at rank 1, handing him a disable-immune all-in or a clean escape from your dive. Don't ult in expecting to be unstoppable - he can answer with your own kit. Fight when Abscond and the stolen R are down.","late":"This is where Sylas pulls ahead. Full-AP, Kingslayer heals through your damage and his two dashes kite you off him while your flat E true damage stops mattering. You can't grind him down once he out-sustains and out-bursts you. Convert your early lead into towers, plates and dives before two items land - if it goes long, he wins the extended fight and turns your own ult against you.","whys":["You both fight melee, but your Q-slow-into-auto and passive attack speed win first contact - Sylas has no early sustain edge yet.","Your E true damage nuke lands before Kingslayer is up to heal the trade back.","Q plus E gives a guaranteed true-damage burst that one Kingslayer heal cannot out-sustain yet.","Axe resets and Tough It Out let you out-grind Chain Lash and Kingslayer in short trades.","Level 6 is even-to-his-favor - his R steals your Ragnarok, so the CC-immune all-in you'd rely on is now his too.","Your bruiser-core all-in still trades with a one-rotation Sylas, but Hijack and his dashes keep it close.","Full-AP Sylas heals through your damage with Kingslayer and kites on two dashes while your true damage falls off."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"tahmkench","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Skill","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks him before Thick Skin has stored enough to matter — your cleanest early all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok blocks his Tongue Lash stun while you keep swinging, so you commit through the tool that peels you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble shred plus your E true damage answer his stacking armor and grey-health healing for one more strong window."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-item Tahm Kench out-sustains your flat true damage with Thick Skin and his total-health passive, and Devour roams better than your splitpush."}],"wants":{"you":["Force level 2-3 all-ins with Q-slow into E true damage before Thick Skin has anything stored","Chain Undertow pickups to perma-slow him so he cannot walk to minions or line up Tongue Lash","Swing through his Tongue Lash stun with Ragnarok while you hold an early gold lead"],"foe":["Soak your E true damage into Thick Skin, then shield it or back off to heal it back","Stack An Acquired Taste to three, then Tongue Lash you for the stun from 900 range","Stall lane even and roam bot with Devour to cash your stalemate elsewhere"]},"early":"Tahm Kench is one of the few melees you can't simply out-trade on stats, because Thick Skin stores a share of everything you land and either converts it to a shield or heals it back once he steps away. Win the early levels anyway: hit your level 2-3 Q-slow into E before that bar is deep, and force the trade while Abyssal Dive is on its 21s cooldown. Don't sit at Tongue Lash range with no follow-up — a third stack of An Acquired Taste turns it into a stun, and eating that for nothing lets him reset the trade.","mid":"Levels 4-6 even out because he stops dying to single combos once Thick Skin is online — every E you land partly feeds a bar he reclaims. Keep stacking short trades with axe resets and Tough It Out's shield so you stay ahead on the wave and bank a CS and plates lead. At 6 Ragnarok matters but is not a blank cheque: it blocks his Tongue Lash stun while you keep attacking, and Abyssal Dive's knockup is a displacement it does not stop, so dive only when you already hold a gold lead.","late":"This is where he takes over. A two-item Tahm Kench heals your flat E true damage back faster than you can re-apply it, Thick Skin turns your biggest hit into a shield, and a passive that scales off his total health out-lasts a short-fight kit like yours. Worse, Devour lets him roam and snowball a second lane off your stalemate while your own splitpush stalls into a tank that won't die. Convert every early-to-mid plate, kill and herald into objectives before two items land — if it goes late, he wins the map.","whys":["Your level-1 Q-slow into auto wins first contact before his grey health is deep enough to absorb it.","At 2 your Q plus E lands a guaranteed true-damage burst he can't out-stat, and Thick Skin has no stored damage to convert yet.","By 3 your axe-reset slows perma-stick him and E chunks through his armor faster than early grey health refills.","Lanes even out as Thick Skin comes online — every Reckless Swing partly feeds a bar he converts to a shield or heals back out of combat.","Ragnarok blocks his Tongue Lash stun while you swing, but Abyssal Dive's knockup is a displacement it ignores — a true coinflip.","Your Cleaver and Bramble spike still pressures his armour stacking, but Thick Skin's stored healing keeps the lane a stalemate.","Two-item Tahm Kench converts your flat true damage into a Thick Skin shield, out-sustains short fights, and roams with Devour."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"teemo","win":["Teemo","Teemo","Teemo","Skill","Teemo","Skill","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Lead with Q to slow him, then auto — your passive attack speed ramps as you take his poke, so first contact already favors you."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks him through the blind — Blinding Dart is 7s, so trade in the gap after he spends it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok does not clear the blind — keep it simple: Q-slow, Reckless Swing true damage, and swing through his kite for the kill."},{"when":"Late","text":"His shrooms zone objectives and he splitpushes safely — your flat E true damage stops mattering, so close before 2+ items."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to perma-slow him so he can't kite, then re-throw on the refunded cooldown to keep him stuck","Eat the blind on autos but land Reckless Swing — Blinding Dart cannot stop it","Snowball levels 2-6 and dive him before his shrooms and splitpush take over the map"],"foe":["Blind your autos with Blinding Dart every trade so your attack-speed ramp does nothing","Kite with Move Quick and Toxic Shot poison, staying outside your 1000 Q range","Survive to stack shrooms on chokes and objectives and splitpush the side lane"]},"early":"Blinding Dart only kills your autos — it does nothing to Reckless Swing, which is point-blank guaranteed true damage. So the early game is about landing your own Q first: throw the axe to slow him, walk up, and E him for a chunk he cannot poke back through. Blinding Dart is 7s flat, so the trade window is the gap right after he spends it. Move Quick lets him kite, but a stuck Q-slow pins him inside 325. And Guerrilla Warfare turns him invisible in brush, so never facecheck one.","mid":"This is your takeover. Every trade is the same: Q to slow, E for true damage, W on for the shield so you eat the poison and swing right back. Blinding Dart is the only thing he has and it cannot stop your E. Pick the axe back up to refund the Q cooldown and re-slow him so he never escapes to kite range. At 6, Ragnarok covers his disables and he has no dash to create distance — the one thing that still peels you is standing in a Noxious Trap, so watch the ground. Run him down on the 7s blind cooldown.","late":"You win the straight 1v1 all game, but Teemo turns into a map problem. His shrooms wall off objectives and brush, and he splitpushes a side lane safely while your flat E true damage and short-fight kit stop scaling. If the game drags past two items he is chipping you from range before you ever land a Q. Win the lane early, snowball the lead into towers and dives, and end it before his scaling and mushroom vision ever come online — never facecheck brush near Dragon or Baron.","whys":["You win first contact — Q-slow into an auto, and Berserker Rage ramps as you take his poke, while Blinding Dart blanks autos but never Reckless Swing.","At 2 you add E for a guaranteed true-damage burst through his blind that his poke can't answer.","Q-slow into E true damage takes half his bar, and picking the axe back up refunds the Q to re-slow him before he kites.","You out-trade his poke with Tough It Out's shield while your slows keep him pinned inside 325 for E.","Ragnarok covers his disables and he has no dash, so Q, E and W run him down — only Noxious Trap slows can save him.","Your bruiser-core spike is your most oppressive lane window; keep forcing the all-in on his blind timer.","He out-scales the duel's relevance — shrooms zone objectives and he splitpushes safely, so close the game before two items."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"trundle","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Skill","Trundle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage is your cleanest window — his Q bite and pillar don't out-trade you before he has sustain stacked."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok is not the answer to Pillar of Ice — that is terrain, not a disable, so walk around it before you commit the all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Subjugate steals a share of your health and resists — including the armour and MR Ragnarok's passive is giving you — for 4 seconds."},{"when":"Late","text":"Chomp saps your attack damage while Frozen Domain amplifies every heal he takes — your flat true damage stops being enough."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow and chain axe pickups to stick him for repeated E true-damage bursts","Force short all-ins at levels 2-6 before his Q-bite AD steal and R sustain stack up","Use Ragnarok to ignore his E pillar and W slow zone and dive him through peel"],"foe":["Land Chomp every 3.5s to sap your AD and blunt every auto trade","Drop Pillar of Ice to wall off your all-in and reset on his terms","Reach Subjugate and items to out-drain your short-fight kit and scale past you"]},"early":"Trundle is one of the few drain-tanks you don't just run over, so respect Chomp — every bite steals your attack damage and it is back up in 3.5s. King's Tribute also heals him off every minion that dies near him, so he is never as low as the bar suggests. Still, levels 1-3 are yours: land Q to slow, walk up, and weave E true damage before his sustain is stacked. Pillar of Ice is 21s at rank 1 — bait it, then commit, because it is terrain you walk around, not CC you push through.","mid":"Levels 4-6 even out as Chomp's AD steal and Frozen Domain's speed and healing amp let him sustain and reposition out of your axe slows. Keep forcing short all-ins where Tough It Out's shield and your E burst beat his raw drain, but don't extend into a fight he can kite with W and reset with a pillar. At 6 Ragnarok is not the equalizer the lane wants: Pillar of Ice is terrain it cannot cancel and Subjugate is a stat theft it cannot block, so time the dive on his cooldowns.","late":"This is where Trundle pulls ahead. Subjugate steals a percent of your health, armour and MR — and Ragnarok's passive resists are part of the pile he takes from — while Chomp chips your AD, so your flat E true damage stops closing the gap. King's Tribute out-sustains you in any extended fight and a pillar zones you off the carries. Convert your early lead into towers, plates and dives before two items — if it goes long and even, his drain-tank scaling quietly wins the lane.","whys":["Your Q-slow-into-auto and passive beat his level-1 — his Q bite only steals a little AD before you've committed any trade.","Your Q plus E lands a guaranteed true-damage burst he can't match with one bite and no sustain.","Axe-reset slows let you chain Q and E him repeatedly before his healing comes online.","Chomp's AD steal and Frozen Domain's healing amp let him sustain — short trades even out, so commit only with W up.","Ragnarok covers disables, but Pillar of Ice is terrain it cannot remove and Subjugate is a stat theft, not CC.","Your bruiser core stays strong, but his R Subjugate and AD steal arrive at the same time — neither side owns the all-in.","Subjugate steals your resists, King's Tribute heals off every dying minion, and his drain-tank scaling out-sustains you."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"tryndamere","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E's true-damage nuke online you can land a guaranteed burst Trynd can't crit back through before he has fury or spin DPS."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok strips his W-slow and lets you ignore his kiting, but his R Undying Rage means you often can't finish the kill even after winning the trade."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble Vest is your most oppressive lane point — perma-slow axes and omnivamp out-grind his pre-crit spin."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Trynd hits Infinity Edge plus crit he spin-kites and survives at 1 HP through your all-in; this window is his."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow so he cannot Spinning Slash back out of your auto range","Reach level 2-3 and open with E's true damage before he stacks fury for crit DPS","Snowball levels 1-5 and end the lane before his Infinity Edge crit spike comes online"],"foe":["Gap-close with Spinning Slash, then make you turn and run so Mocking Shout slows","Survive your all-in with Undying Rage, then heal it all back with Bloodlust","Scale to Infinity Edge crit so Spinning Slash out-DPSes your flat true damage"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are yours. Your Q axe slows him so he can't spin away, and once you have E you land a guaranteed true-damage chunk his pre-Fury autos can't match. Open trades with Q to stick the slow, then walk in for E and let your passive ramp attack speed as you take a little damage back. Mocking Shout only slows enemies whose backs are turned, so never retreat through it — face him. And the heal is Bloodlust (12s), which spends his Fury: short decisive trades beat him, drawn-out ones pay for it.","mid":"This is your strongest stretch — keep forcing short all-ins. Chain Q throws to perma-slow him, W for the shield, and E true damage straight through his health bar; his crit isn't online yet so you out-trade and out-sustain. At 6 be honest about Undying Rage: even a perfectly won trade often ends with him surviving on a sliver and spinning away, and Ragnarok does nothing about that — it covers disables, not his immortality. Burn the ultimate if you must, then dive with your jungler before its 120s is back.","late":"This window flips to him. Once Trynd stacks Infinity Edge and crit, Spinning Slash out-DPSes your flat true damage and Undying Rage erases your all-in outright. Your job was to make the game end before this — convert your level 1-to-6 lead into towers, dives and objectives so his scaling never gets to matter. In a straight late-game 1v1 he wins; don't isolate yourself splitpushing into a fed Trynd. Group, and let your team's CC land in the window right after his ultimate ends.","whys":["Your Q-slow-into-auto and passive win first contact; Spinning Slash has no Fury and no crit to answer it.","At 2 you add the second ability and your Q-slow keeps him from dropping back to spin-kite.","E's guaranteed true damage on top of a Q-slow is a burst his pre-crit autos simply can't trade back.","You snowball short trades with axe resets and Tough It Out while Bloodlust's healing cannot outpace your burst.","Mocking Shout only slows you if your back is turned, so face him and walk in — but Undying Rage still denies the kill.","Your Black Cleaver core perma-slows and out-grinds a Trynd without Infinity Edge, but his R still saves him.","With crit online he spin-kites, out-DPSes your true damage, and Undying Rage survives your all-in — this is his window."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"urgot","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Undertow into Reckless Swing bursts him with true damage while Disdain is down — 16s at rank 1, and it is his only way out."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok cleanses his W shotgun-leg slow, his E flip and his R fear — you become unstoppable and run him down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver + Bramble Vest: your most oppressive window — shred his armor and cut his Stridebreaker/Death's Dance healing."},{"when":"Late","text":"Urgot's biggest threat: rank 5 Purge is free with no cooldown, so Echoing Flames grinds you down in any long brawl."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick Undertow's slow so he can't walk out of your range, then Reckless Swing him for true damage","Force short all-ins at Lvl 2-3 and 6 before his percent-HP DPS ramps over a long fight","Buy Bramble Vest early to cut the healing he gets from Stridebreaker and Death's Dance"],"foe":["Drag fights long — rank 5 Purge is free with no cooldown and Echoing Flames keeps ticking","Land E flip + R fear to peel your all-in and reset the trade out of your Q range","Sit back and farm with Corrosive Charge from 800 range, denying the melee range you need"]},"early":"Urgot wants to farm and chip with Purge, but it reaches only 490 and slows him while it fires, so he cannot punish you at Level 1. At Level 2-3 throw Undertow to slow him, walk in, and Reckless Swing his face for true damage his armour does nothing about. Pick the axe back up — that refunds the 9s cooldown, so you chain slows and he never walks out of range. Don't spend Reckless Swing on chip: it costs your own health, refunded only on the kill.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep snowballing short trades — Q-slow, W for omnivamp and attack speed, E to chunk, and your passive ramps faster as you take his shotgun-leg damage. Level 6 is your kill window: Ragnarok cleanses his E flip, W slow and R fear all at once, so he loses every tool that peels you and you just run him down. With Black Cleaver and Bramble Vest you're at your most oppressive — shred his armor and cut the healing he leans on.","late":"This is where Urgot reclaims relevance. Maxed Purge costs nothing and has no cooldown at all, so Echoing Flames ticks nonstop and a long brawl beats your one-shot Reckless Swing — exactly the fight he wants and you don't. Fear Beyond Death reaches 2500 and executes you for committing low, so stay above the threshold. Convert your early-to-mid lead into towers, plates and dives before this window; don't let a 50-minute game arrive where his uptime and tankiness beat your short-fight kit.","whys":["Undertow into autos wins first contact — Purge is only 490 range and slows him while it fires, so he can't poke free.","Q plus E lands a guaranteed true-damage burst he can only answer with slowed shotgun autos.","Axe-reset slows let you chain Q and chunk him with E before he can angle his W cone.","You out-trade his pokes with W omnivamp and a passive that ramps as his shotgun legs hit you.","Ragnarok cleanses his E flip, W slow and R fear — unstoppable, you all-in or dive him.","Black Cleaver and Bramble Vest shred his armor and cut his Stridebreaker/Death's Dance healing.","Rank 5 Purge costs nothing and has no cooldown, so his Echoing Flames DPS beats your burst."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"vayne","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Vayne"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E's true-damage nuke online you can land a guaranteed burst Vayne has no early answer to before her W bolts ramp."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok answers Condemn's stun and axe slows run her down — Tumble is 6s at rank 1, so she cannot dash out of it twice."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble core makes your perma-slow all-ins oppressive while she is still one item from her hypercarry power spike."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-plus items in, Silver Bolts' percent-max-HP true damage and tumble-invis kiting flip the duel — she shreds you faster than W-omnivamp heals."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow, then E her for guaranteed true damage before she tumbles out of range","Force short all-ins at 2-6 where her W bolts need three hits to ramp and yours bursts now","Snowball the early lead into towers and objectives before her item spikes arrive"],"foe":["Kite back with Q tumble-invis and chip you with autos so you never land a clean Q-E","Save Condemn (E) to peel your all-in or stun-cancel your gap-close into a wall","Reach two-plus items so Silver Bolts' true damage melts you through W-omnivamp"]},"early":"Vayne is one of the weakest level-1 laners in the game and you are one of the strongest, so step up and make first contact hurt. Land Q to slow her, walk on top, and weave autos — your passive ramps attack speed as you take her chip, so the lower you both get the worse it is for her. The instant you hit level 2-3 with Q plus E, you can throw the axe, walk in, and detonate E's guaranteed true damage for a burst her three-stack Silver Bolts can't trade back. Don't chase a tumble blindly — bait her Q dash, then commit when it's down.","mid":"This is your takeover window. Pick the axe back up to refund Undertow's 9s cooldown and perma-slow her so she can never kite the trade, then Reckless Swing for the true-damage chunk while W's shield eats her return fire. At 6 Ragnarok is the key: press it as she Condemns and the disable immunity answers her stun, then chain axe slows onto a Tumble that is only 6s at rank 1. Keep forcing all-ins on her cooldowns — every short fight is one her ramping Silver Bolts loses.","late":"Be honest with yourself: this is where Vayne takes the lane back. Two-plus items in, her Silver Bolts deal percent-max-HP true damage every third hit and her tumble-invis lets her reset distance faster than you can re-stick Q, so a straight duel flips hard against you. Your flat E true damage and short-fight kit lose value exactly as her DPS scales infinitely. The whole game is a race: convert your early-to-mid dominance into towers, plates, and dives now, and make sure the map is decided before her items come online.","whys":["Vayne is among the weakest level-1s and you are among the strongest — Q-slow into autos wins first contact outright.","Undertow plus your ramping passive sticks her before Silver Bolts reaches its third hit, and Condemn is 20s.","With Q and E online you land a guaranteed true-damage burst she has no early tool to answer.","Axe-reset perma-slow plus W-omnivamp out-sustains her tumble-and-chip kiting through levels 4-5.","Ragnarok answers her Condemn stun and your axe slow closes the Tumble gap — this is your all-in window.","Your Black Cleaver / Bramble spike is oppressive while she's still one item short of her power curve — but she's close, so it's a coinflip.","She out-scales hard: Silver Bolts' percent-HP true damage and invis kiting shred you faster than W can heal — play for the early lead instead."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"vladimir","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Undertow into Reckless Swing chunks a Vlad with no pool — it is 28s at rank 1."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"He has no hard CC for Ragnarok to answer, but pool is 28s: bait it, then Reckless Swing him as he surfaces."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Bramble Vest plus your bruiser core fights his Q-Rylai sustain, but his W untargetability starts blanking your E."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-AP Vlad pools your all-in, Q-heals it back and bursts you — his strongest window, avoid the solo."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick the Undertow slow, then Reckless Swing him before Sanguine Pool (28s) is back","Force short all-ins at 2-3 and 6 where his cooldowns leave him with no escape","Snowball the early lead into towers and objectives before his AP items come online"],"foe":["Pool (W) your E and committed all-in, then walk out untargetable","Poke with E and heal with Q to win the long game without ever fully trading","Stall to 2-3 items where Rylai and AP burst flip the duel and teamfights"]},"early":"Vlad is one of the weakest level-1s in the game and so are you, but you ramp faster — your passive gives attack speed as you take his E poke, and your Q-slow lets you stick to him for a free auto. The key is he has no escape until W Sanguine Pool, so levels 2-3 are your kill window: Q to slow, E for the guaranteed true-damage chunk, and his Q heal can't out-sustain a committed Olaf. Don't waste E on minions and don't let his E poke stack you down while you sit passive — step up and trade, you win every short exchange here.","mid":"This is still your lane. Keep baiting his W — pool is 28s at rank 1, so once it is gone he has no answer to Undertow into Reckless Swing, with your passive life steal ramping as you drop low. At 6 he has no hard CC for Ragnarok to strip, but it still lets you commit and chase; hold Reckless Swing until the instant he surfaces, because 2 seconds of untargetable eats it whole. Force these fights NOW and convert kills into plates and dives — every minute you delay, his Rylai's and AP items pull the lane back to him.","late":"He out-scales you hard and this is where the 47% lives. Full-AP Vlad pools your entire commit, Q-heals back whatever you chunked, and E-Q bursts you from range while Rylai's slows you off him. Your flat true damage and short-fight kit lose value the moment he has two items. Don't take the solo sidelane fight late — group, use your Ragnarok to dive his carries in teamfights instead of dueling him, and rely on the early lead you should already have to have ended the game.","whys":["Vlad is one of the weakest level-1s, but your Q-slow and passive attack-speed win first contact even in a mutually weak opener.","No Sanguine Pool yet, and it is 28s at rank 1 — land Undertow, auto, set up level 3.","Q-slow into E true damage chunks him hard and his Q heal can't match it before pool exists.","You out-trade a pre-Rylai Vlad — bait the 28s Sanguine Pool, then commit Undertow into Reckless Swing.","Ragnarok lets you fully commit and run him down; E him the instant he surfaces from pool for the kill.","It is even now — Bramble and your bruiser core still fight, but his W untargetability and first AP item start eating your E.","Full-AP Vlad pools your all-in, heals it with Q and bursts you down — play safe and let your team handle him."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"volibear","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks Voli before his W bite-heal can sustain it back — your hardest early all-in window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok answers Thundering Smash — his Q stun is his only hard CC and it is 12s, so bait it, press R and dive him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble Vest — Bramble cuts his W-bite omnivamp and Cleaver shreds his armor; your most oppressive lane state."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Voli's biggest threat window — tank items plus a 5s Frenzied Maul heal reclaim the brawl once your flat true damage stops mattering."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slow then E for guaranteed true damage before his W bite-heal ticks back up","All-in at 6 — Ragnarok ignores his E stun so his peel is wasted","Stack Bramble Vest early to gut his W omnivamp and close the lane before 2 items"],"foe":["Land Thundering Smash, his Q stun, to lock your all-in before you swing","Sustain through trades with W bite-heal and stall to his tank-item scaling","Use Stormbringer's leap and tower disable to dive you back once he out-tanks you"]},"early":"Voli is a tanky even-brawler, but you out-trade him 1-3 because Reckless Swing is true damage his armour and Frenzied Maul heal cannot soak. Land Undertow to slow him, walk up for an auto, and swing when he steps to last-hit — your passive ramps attack speed as you drop low. The ability that flips a trade is Thundering Smash, his Q stun on 12s: sidestep that wind-up, not Sky Splitter, which only slows and shields him.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep snowballing short trades — the axe pickup refunds Undertow's 9s cooldown so he can never disengage, and your passive life steal answers his bite. At 6 you hit a wall-breaker: Ragnarok's disable immunity eats Thundering Smash, the Q stun that is his only hard CC, so the ability he needs to peel or engage does nothing. Bait that 12s stun first, then ult and run him down or dive.","late":"This is where Voli reclaims it. He builds tank, his W bite-heal and passive sustain make him an unkillable front-line, and your flat true damage stops one-shotting him once he has health and resists. His R disables your tower and his E-stun engage now out-brawls your short-fight kit. You must convert the early lead into kills, plates, and Herald before two items — if it goes even into late, the scaling tank wins.","whys":["Your Q-slow-into-auto and passive beat his first contact — he has no level-1 burst to answer it.","Your level-2 Q+E lands guaranteed true damage his W bite-heal can't sustain through.","With Q, W and E online you out-trade him — axe-reset slows stick and omnivamp wins the exchange.","You snowball short trades; Bramble/early armor blunt his W omnivamp so his sustain plan fails.","Ragnarok answers Thundering Smash, his Q stun on 12s — his only lockdown is dead while you dive.","Your Black Cleaver/Bramble spike out-paces his — Cleaver shreds his armor and Bramble cuts his bite-heal.","He out-scales hard: tank items and his E-stun engage reclaim the brawl as your true damage falls off — close it before then."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"warwick","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true damage chunks him for a guaranteed burst his passive heal cannot recoup at full HP."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is 110s for 1.5s of suppression — Ragnarok answers it, so he spends his ult and dies for it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble Vest: Bramble's Grievous Wounds caps his passive lifesteal exactly when you out-trade hardest."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past 2 items Warwick's sustained drain and chase out-heal your flat E true damage — his scaling reclaims the duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick the Undertow slow, then Reckless Swing before Blood Hunt turns on under 50% HP","Force short all-ins at Levels 2-6 where your passive attack speed and life steal out-burst his drain","Buy Bramble Vest early so Grievous Wounds halves his passive low-HP healing in every trade"],"foe":["Drag fights long so his Q heal and low-HP passive lifesteal out-sustain your burst","Hit Level 6 to land R suppress and lock you for his jungler to collapse","Break your stick with Primal Howl's fear, then Blood Hunt back onto you once you are low"]},"early":"Warwick is one of the weakest level-1s and has no answer to Undertow into autos — stick the axe, walk him down, and deny him free Jaws of the Beast heals off minions. At Levels 2-3 Reckless Swing is the whole lane: true damage ignores his bulk, and above 50% health Eternal Hunger does not heal him at all. Trade short and pick the axe back up — the 9s cooldown refunds, so Primal Howl's 1s fear buys him nothing.","mid":"Keep forcing short all-ins — your passive ramps attack speed and life steal as you take his drain damage, and a pre-6 Warwick loses the sustain race he thinks he owns. The danger window is Level 6: Infinite Duress is 110s and holds you for 1.5 seconds, which is exactly long enough for his jungler. Bait it, or hold Ragnarok and press yours as he leaps so the disable immunity answers the suppress, then Reckless Swing him while he is committed.","late":"This is where Warwick flips it: past two items his low-HP passive lifesteal and Q heal out-sustain your flat E true damage in any extended fight, and his W lets him chase you forever. Don't try to outduel a fed Warwick in a long fight — your kit is short-burst and his only gets stronger the longer it drags. Close the lane before then, snowball the early lead into towers and objectives, and keep Bramble Vest's Grievous Wounds on him whenever you do commit.","whys":["He is one of the weakest level-1s and your Q-slow-into-auto wins first contact while his passive heal does nothing at full HP.","Q plus E lands a guaranteed true-damage burst he can't sustain through this early — chunk him before his Q heal matters.","Axe resets keep him stuck; his only peel is Primal Howl's 1s fear on 15s, and true damage ignores his bulk.","Your passive attack speed and life steal win the short trade his drain wants long — Blood Hunt is 80s.","Ragnarok cleanses his R suppress mid-channel: he commits his ult, you walk out CC-immune, and E finishes him.","Your Bramble/Cleaver spike with Grievous Wounds caps his passive lifesteal exactly when your lane pressure peaks.","Past two items his drain and W chase out-heal your flat true damage in a long fight — don't duel him, play for objectives."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"wukong","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill","Skill","Skill","Wukong"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into auto plus a guaranteed E true-damage hit lands before Wukong has his Q armor-shred online — your cleanest early kill window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok cleanses his R spin knockup mid-cast, so you can ult through his all-in and keep swinging instead of getting tossed."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver plus Bramble at your lane-bully peak — chunk him with Reckless Swing and let W's shield eat his answer."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Wukong has 2+ items his clone burst and R knockup in teamfights outscale your flat true damage — close before then."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to stick the slow, then E-W all-in before his Q armor-shred and dash reset the trade","Use your level 2-3 true-damage burst to bully him before his clone and shred come online","Ragnarok answers his Cyclone knockup — it is 100s at rank 1, so spend it only on a kill"],"foe":["Bait your E or Q on his W clone decoy, then dash in with E on the real target","Stack armor and Q armor-shred to blunt your auto trades and grind you out item-dependent","Land R spin knockup when your Ragnarok is on cooldown to lock you for his burst"]},"early":"Wukong has no clone yet and his Q armor-shred is single-rank, so the first three levels are yours. Land Q to slow him, walk up, and weave an E true-damage hit the moment he commits to a creep or steps for a trade. Watch his E dash range, that is his only reset tool early, and do not waste your Q on a clone he has not made yet. If he greeds a last hit at melee range, your level 2-3 Q-E-W is a chunk he simply cannot trade back.","mid":"Levels 4-6 even out as Warrior Trickster comes online and Crushing Blow shreds your armor, so respect the juke. The clone mimics his animations — do not spend Undertow or Reckless Swing on the decoy, wait the half-second to confirm the real Wukong. At 6 Ragnarok is the answer to his all-in: press it as he casts Cyclone and the knockup does nothing, leaving you free to swing while your passive life steal ramps and his burst fizzles.","late":"This is where Wukong takes over. Stacked armor blunts your autos, Crushing Blow's shred and the clone let him burst you in a teamfight, and Cyclone catches you the moment Ragnarok's 100 seconds are down. Your flat true damage and short-fight kit lose value while he scales item-dependent. Build Bramble and push your early-to-mid lead into towers and objectives, because if the game goes long his clone-and-knockup combo wins the fights yours can no longer reach.","whys":["No clone and only one rank of Q armor-shred yet, so your Q-slow-into-auto and passive ramp win first contact clean.","Your level 2 Q plus E lands a guaranteed true-damage burst before his clone or shred can answer it.","Q-E-W chains a slow and true damage he cannot trade back while his only reset is a short E dash.","His W clone and Q armor-shred come online and start blunting your autos, leveling the short trades out.","Ragnarok cleanses his R spin knockup so neither of you cleanly wins the all-in, but you remove his best tool.","Your Black Cleaver and Bramble peak matches his first-item clone spike, keeping the lane a coinflip.","His stacked armor, clone burst and R knockup outscale your flat true damage once he hits 2+ items."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"yasuo","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once you have Q plus E, an axe-slow into Reckless Swing true damage chunks him before he can stack flow shield or build crit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok cleanses his R knockup and ignores it mid-fight, so you all-in through the one tool that lets him reset onto you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver / Bramble core is your peak lane-pressure window — perma-slow him with axe resets and run him down before his crit items come online."},{"when":"Late","text":"At 2+ crit items Wind Wall is down to 17s, so it eats an axe every fight and he kites your short-fight kit apart."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-slows and pick the axe back up to chain-slow him, then E true damage before he builds crit","Force melee all-ins where your passive attack speed and life steal ramp faster than his early trades do","Hit Level 6 and use Ragnarok to ignore his R knockup and dive him before his items come online"],"foe":["Hold Wind Wall's 25s to delete your axe so the slow never sets up your swing","Dash through minions with his Q-stacks to dodge your axe and avoid committing until he has crit","Survive lane and reach 2+ crit items where his sustained DPS and mobility outrun your short fight"]},"early":"Yasuo can't punch with you levels 1-3 — Undertow into autos wins first contact and his early trades have no sustain. Throw the axe, walk up, pick it back up to keep him slowed, then weave an auto so your passive ramps. Wind Wall is the whole dance: 25s at rank 1, and it deletes the axe outright, so if he walls it, just farm. Bait the wall on the wave and your next axe sticks for the full 25 seconds.","mid":"This is your lane. With Black Cleaver and Bramble online your axe resets perma-slow him while your passive life steal answers his crit autos, and Reckless Swing's true damage cuts through the Flow shield. At 6 he cannot cast Last Breath unless something puts you airborne, so the thing to dodge is the two-stack Steel Tempest whirlwind — and Ragnarok answers it anyway. Dive him on Wind Wall's 25s cooldown and keep every fight short and melee, where your ramping attack speed wins.","late":"You own this lane, but Yasuo is the textbook scaler who reclaims the late game. Once he has 2+ crit items he kites your short-fight kit, Windwall blanks your Q on cooldown so your slow never sticks, and his DPS plus dash mobility outrun your flat true damage. Your job is to make the late game never happen — convert your level-1-to-6 lead into kills, plates, and grubs/Herald, and end before his crit build comes online.","whys":["Your Q-slow into auto wins first contact and his earliest trade has no flow shield or crit to answer your passive ramp.","Once you add E to Q, axe-slow into Reckless Swing true damage chunks him before he can stack any defense.","Chained axe pickups perma-slow him while your passive life steal answers the crit autos he trades back.","Black Cleaver lets you stick short trades; W shields the burst and your passive heals you back.","Ragnarok cleanses and ignores his R knockup, killing the reset tool he needs — you all-in through it.","Your bruiser core is at peak lane pressure; perma-slow and dive him before his crit items exist.","At 2+ crit items Wind Wall is a 17s answer to every axe and he kites your short-fight kit into the ground."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"yone","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q-slow into E true-damage burst chunks Yone before his Q-stacks or W damage ramp — your hardest early window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok cleanses his R knockup mid-air, so you keep diving while he's airborne and can't peel."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver and Bramble — chained axe resets mean his two-stack Mortal Steel dash never buys him spacing."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Yone's window: full crit and a 10s Soul Unbound let him reset every trade and outscale your damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q on him so the slow sticks and his Q-dash can't reset spacing, then E for the true-damage chunk","Force short all-ins at 2-6 where W's shield and your ramping passive beat his Spirit Cleave trades","Save Ragnarok to cleanse his R knockup so a roam or all-in converts into a kill before items"],"foe":["Use the Mortal Steel dash and Soul Unbound's snap-back to reset to safe range between trades","Stack his Q and ramp W damage in extended fights instead of taking your short bursts","Reach 2+ crit items where his mobility and steroids outscale your flat true damage and short kit"]},"early":"Yone is genuinely even at level 1, but you spike harder fast. Land Undertow to slow him, walk up, and weave an auto — by 2-3 you add Reckless Swing for a true-damage chunk he cannot match before Mortal Steel stacks or Spirit Cleave ramps. Don't throw the axe into his two-stack dash. Bait Soul Unbound early: it is 22s at rank 1, and once it is gone he has no way out of your all-in.","mid":"This is your takeover. Your passive ramps attack speed and life steal as you take his cleave damage, W's shield eats the rest, and chained axe resets keep him perma-slowed. At 6 Ragnarok is the key beat — press it as he ults so Fate Sealed's pull does nothing and you keep swinging. Soul Unbound is 22s at rank 1: the moment he spends it, he has no way out of your all-in. Force every fight in this window.","late":"Yone reclaims the game at 2+ items. Full crit plus his E spirit-rewind let him reset every trade, dodge your committed Q, and bleed you out where your flat E true damage stops scaling. Don't sidelane him even in a straight 1v1 once he's two items deep — he kites your slow and outDPS-es your short kit. Your job was already done: convert the early-to-mid lead into towers, dives, and objectives before this window arrives, so his scaling never gets to matter.","whys":["Even at 1, but your Q-slow-into-auto wins first contact before his Q stacks or W ramps.","Your level-2 Q+E gives a guaranteed true-damage chunk he can't trade back into.","Q-slow sticks him and E true damage bursts him before his cleave damage ramps in extended fights.","Axe resets perma-slow him while W's shield eats Spirit Cleave, which is only 14s.","Ragnarok cleanses his R knockup mid-air — you keep all-in diving while he can't peel.","Black Cleaver and Bramble make the slow constant, so his 4s Mortal Steel dash buys nothing.","Full crit plus E-rewind resets let him kite your slow and outscale your flat true damage — sidelane is lost."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"yorick","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E's true damage you land a guaranteed burst Yorick's ghoul-walls can't shield, before Maiden exists."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok answers Mourning Mist's slow and the Dark Procession cage is destructible — 20s of wall he wastes."},{"when":"1st item","text":"On Bramble/Black Cleaver your dive is at its peak — force every all-in before Maiden timers and ghoul stacks make his trades free."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Yorick's window: full Maiden plus ghoul army out-DPS your flat true damage and he splits the map you can't 1v1-stop."}],"wants":{"you":["Hit your Level 2-3 Q-slow into E true-damage burst before Maiden and the ghoul wall come online","Use Ragnarok at 6 to ignore Mourning Mist's slow and force the melee all-in he can't escape","Snowball lane and take Yorick's tower/plates before his 2-item splitpush scaling reclaims the game"],"foe":["Stack ghouls and summon Maiden so every trade adds free damage you can't out-sustain","Mark you with Mourning Mist and cage you with Dark Procession while the ghouls chip you","Survive to 2 items and splitpush the side lane where his Maiden + cage win the 1v1"]},"early":"Yorick is slow and immobile at Levels 1-3 with no escape, which is exactly your meal. Land Undertow to slow him, walk up, and Reckless Swing for guaranteed true damage — hit him before graves turn into ghouls or Maiden exists. The ability to respect is Mourning Mist (E): it shreds your armour, slows you, and marks you so every ghoul sprints straight at you. Dark Procession is the cage, 20s at rank 1 and destructible — swing it down rather than walking the long way round.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep snowballing short trades — axe resets perma-slow him so he can't walk out, and W's shield eats whatever the ghouls poke off you. At 6 Ragnarok is the whole lane: it answers Mourning Mist's slow, so the moment he tries to zone you off the wave, ult and run him down — he has no hard CC to stop you in melee. Bait that E first; it is 12s at rank 1, and once it is gone the ghouls lose their mark and he is a sitting target.","late":"This is where Yorick takes over and you have to be honest about it. By 2+ items his full Maiden plus a permanent ghoul army out-DPS your flat true damage, and he splits a side lane your kit can't 1v1-stop — his E cage and wall trap you while the swarm shreds you. Your flat E and short-fight all-ins lose value here, so you must have already converted: take his plates and tower early, snowball your lead into objectives, and end before his splitpush and Maiden timers make the game his.","whys":["Yorick is a slow immobile melee with no level-1 escape — your Q-slow-into-auto and passive win first contact before any ghoul or Maiden exists.","Undertow into Reckless Swing lands true damage his cage can't stop, and Dark Procession is 20s at rank 1.","Axe-reset slows keep him stuck in E range for a second true-damage nuke he can't sustain through without Maiden.","You out-trade a pre-Maiden Yorick — W's shield eats the ghoul chip and your slows deny his retreat.","Ragnarok removes his E mist-cage and W wall and grants immunity to all his CC, so he can't zone or kite you out of the all-in.","Your Bramble/Black Cleaver dive spike beats his first-item Yorick before the ghoul army and Maiden snowball — force it now.","He out-scales hard: full Maiden plus the ghoul swarm out-DPS your flat true damage and his cage-and-split wins the side lane — play for an early lead and end before this."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"zac","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"With Q-slow plus E's true-damage nuke you out-burst a Zac whose only answer is reblobbing passive blobs you can deny by standing on them."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok answers his Q grab and E knock-up, and Elastic Slingshot is 21s at rank 1 — bait it, then dive."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver into your true-damage E shreds his stacked tank HP — this is your most oppressive lane-pressure window."},{"when":"Late","text":"Zac's biggest threat: at 2+ items Elastic Slingshot is down to 9s, so his engage and Let's Bounce peel for his carries every fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Stand on his Cell Division chunks so he can't collect them and heal between trades","Land Q-slow and chain axe pickups to perma-stick him, then E for guaranteed true damage","All-in at 6 under Ragnarok so his E knock-up and Q grab do nothing"],"foe":["Collect his Cell Division chunks to out-sustain your short trades","Land long-range E knock-up to start a trade on his terms, not yours","Stall lane and scale to teamfights where his AOE CC peels for carries"]},"early":"Zac is an off-meta top with no early kill threat on you, and you own first contact: Undertow into autos, then your passive ramps attack speed as you trade. The key is Cell Division — every time he lands an ability he sheds a chunk that heals him if he collects it, so stand on the chunks and he gets nothing back. At 2-3 Undertow plus Reckless Swing is a true-damage burst he can't match while the sustain he needs is under your feet.","mid":"This is your takeover. Bait Elastic Slingshot — 21s at rank 1 — and once it is gone you walk in, Undertow to stick him, and let W's shield eat his answer. At 6 Ragnarok is the dagger: it answers his Q grab and the E knock-up, and Unstable Matter carries no CC at all, so nothing peels you off him. With Black Cleaver and Bramble your true damage cuts straight through his stacked HP.","late":"You win the lane hard, but Zac's value flips at 2+ items: Elastic Slingshot becomes a teamfight engage on a 9s cooldown and Let's Bounce knocks up everyone it lands on, while your flat true damage and short-fight kit lose punch against full builds. So cash your lead now — take plates, dive him off Ragnarok, and force objectives before the game becomes a teamfight where his disruption beats your duel.","whys":["You win first contact: Q-slow into auto and your low-HP attack-speed passive beat anything Zac can do at level 1.","Q plus E gives you a guaranteed true-damage burst, and you deny his passive blobs so he can't reheal the trade.","Chained Q axe-pickups perma-slow him while E's true damage shreds his early tank HP faster than blobs restore it.","Short trades favour your passive life steal over his chunk recovery once you stand on the pieces.","Ragnarok answers his Q grab and E knock-up — Unstable Matter has no CC at all to stop the dive.","Black Cleaver plus your true-damage E is your most oppressive window against his stacked, blob-reliant HP.","Zac reclaims this window: his long-range E engage and AOE peel scale up while your flat true damage falls off."]},
  {"a":"olaf","b":"ziggs","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once you have Q-slow plus E's true-damage nuke, a single axe-stick into E chunks Ziggs harder than his bomb can answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok answers his Satchel knockback and the minefield slow — bait that 20s Satchel and he has no exit left."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Black Cleaver plus your axe-reset perma-slow is your most oppressive window — he cannot create the gap his poke needs."},{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Ziggs' threat: his long-range Q bomb chunks you before you have E, so eating poke walking up is his only real lane window."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q to slow Ziggs, pick the axe back up for the cooldown refund, and chain-slow him into E range","Hit Level 2-3 fast to combo Q-slow into E's guaranteed true damage before his poke adds up","Use Ragnarok at 6 to ignore his W knockback and E slow and run him down to the tower"],"foe":["Keep maximum range and land Q bombs on you as you walk up, never letting you close","Drop Hexplosive Minefield on chokes and Satchel to reset the gap after you ult","Stall lane and shove with siege poke so he can roam and out-scale into teamfights"]},"early":"Level 1 is the only awkward part: Ziggs chucks Bouncing Bomb at you from 850 while you walk up to farm, and you have no tool to answer poke yet, so take CS at max range and eat the chip. The lane flips at 2-3 — with Undertow plus Reckless Swing you land the axe, pick it up for the 9s refund, and chain a second slow into true damage. His only exit is Satchel Charge, 20s at rank 1, and once he spends it he is stuck with you.","mid":"This is your takeover. Every time he steps up to poke or push, you Undertow him, walk on top with axe resets, and W's shield eats the minefield chip while Reckless Swing carves a chunk out of his squishy frame. At 6 Ragnarok is the answer to his whole kit — it takes the Satchel knockback and the minefield slow, so you charge straight through the zone and all-in. With Black Cleaver and perma-slow online, he cannot make the gap his poke needs.","late":"You own this lane from 2 through your first item, so the job is to convert it before the game leaves your hands. From 2+ items your flat true damage and short-fight kit fade while Ziggs' artillery scales into a safe siege threat that pokes from screens away. Snowball the early kills into tower plates and dives, and force the game to end or take objectives before he gets to out-range you in every fight from max bomb range.","whys":["Level 1 you have no answer to Bouncing Bomb at 850 range, so he chips you as you walk up to farm — genuinely his window.","With Q-slow and E online you stick him and land guaranteed true damage his single bomb cannot trade back.","Axe-reset slows let you chain a second Undertow into E before his Q cooldown is up, and he has no dash to escape.","W's shield eats the Hexplosive Minefield chip while short axe-reset trades out-damage his poke at 4-5.","Ragnarok cleanses his W knockback and E slow, so you ignore his entire zone and all-in him uncontested.","Black Cleaver plus perma-slow is your peak — he cannot open the distance his artillery poke depends on.","From 2+ items your true damage falls off and his bomb out-ranges you from safety, so the late game neutralizes your dive."]}
