window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"olaf","b":"locke","win":["Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Q slow into E true damage — full trade pattern online"},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok deletes his CC and escape tools"},{"when":"1st item","text":"Bruiser sustain tanks his burst while E chunks him"},{"text":"Careful here: Reckless Swing pays health for its true damage and his passive hits harder the lower you drop — straight into Purgatory's execute.","when":"2+ items"}],"wants":{"you":["Axe fights on every pickup","All-ins whenever he oversteps","Ragnarok pressed through his CC"],"foe":["Distance from your axes","Burst windows your sustain cannot refund","Avoiding you entirely late"]},"early":"Run the lane over: you win level 1 flat, W lifesteal refunds whatever poke he lands, and once Q-slow-into-E is online at 3 he cannot take a trade or leave one. Fight on every axe pickup, chase exchanges through the minion wave and make him play scared from the very first wave onward.","mid":"Nothing changes at 4-5 except the margin — axe pressure and sustain keep him suppressed, so start hunting actual kill windows. At 6, Ragnarok removes every slow and piece of CC he would use to escape: commit the all-in whenever he steps past the halfway line and simply run him down.","late":"You beat his build at every stage — unstoppable Ragnarok plus true damage means no reset, no kite, no escape. Force the sidelane duel, ult through his opener, and in teamfights press R the moment his CC comes out; a squishy execute pattern has no answer to a man who cannot be stopped.","whys":["Level 1 you out-damage and out-sustain his poke — walk at him and start swinging.","Level 2 your base kit and Berserker Rage lifesteal keep every trade yours — his chip heals right back.","At 3, Q slow into E true damage locks the trade pattern in your favour — he cannot kite what he cannot outrun.","Levels 4-5 your sustain and axe pressure keep him pinned on the back foot — keep the axes flying.","Level 6 Ragnarok blanks his disables while you keep swinging — his escape plan stops existing.","First item your bruiser sustain tanks his burst while E chunks him — the trades are not close.","Late, Ragnarok plus true damage beats his squishy build — but never sit low near Purgatory."]});
