window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"olaf","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen","Skill","Skill","Zaahen","Zaahen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"A landed axe plus reclaim lets you stick and trade evenly"},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ragnarok makes your all-in genuinely threatening"},{"when":"With jungle help","text":"Unstoppable dives cash far better than solo duels"},{"text":"Zaahen's window: a filled Determination bar gives him bonus AD and a revive, so anti-heal and kill him with the wave, never in a solo brawl.","when":"2+ items"}],"wants":{"you":["Axes landed before committing","All-ins only off a connected slow","Skirmishes over long solo duels"],"foe":["Chip you inside your 9s axe cooldown","Extended no-CC trades late","Dodging Undertow to erase your kit"]},"early":"Respect his windows: every time your axe misses or sits its 9 seconds, his 850-range stab pulls you in for free, and by 3 his walk-up trades beat yours. Throw Undertow at last-hit timings and pickup angles rather than hope, and keep the wave close so his spacing game has less room to breathe.","mid":"Landing the axe changes everything at 4-5 — slow, stick and trade back with true damage while W's shield covers his answer. At 6 Ragnarok is for his Q recast knockup and his W pull, but he still out-fights a whiffed engage, so commit off a landed Undertow and never off a prayer.","late":"He out-scales you in exactly the fight your kit forces — long, CC-less slugfests — so stop offering them. Take skirmishes with teammates nearby, use Ragnarok to dive backlines instead of dueling him, and cash your unstoppability in fights where it matters more than out-trading one bruiser.","whys":["Level 1 is a neutral farm start — without a reclaimed axe you do not threaten much yet.","At 2 his 850-range pull punishes you every time Undertow is down — the axe cooldown is his window.","At 3 a dodged axe leaves you with zero CC and he wins the walk-up trade — his spacing beats your throw.","Levels 4-5 even out — a landed Undertow plus the reclaimed axe lets you stick to him and trade back properly.","Level 6 is even — Ragnarok's CC immunity and stats make your all-in genuinely threatening, but he can still out-fight a whiffed engage.","By first item he out-spaces and out-sustains you inside the axe-cooldown windows — the duel drifts his way.","Late he scales slightly harder and wins the extended no-CC trades your kit forces — pick fights with numbers, not pride."]});
